r","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nayaksomkar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nayaksomkar/CompetitorEngine/commits/618bcec64c70b5668731f059ad350421c16f81e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:26:01Z","email":"nayaksomkar@outlook.in","name":"Nayak Omkar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:26:01Z","email":"nayaksomkar@outlook.in","name":"Nayak Omkar"},"message":"docs(services): document live LLMPing + WebHunter contracts\n\nTested both independent services directly against their live\nRender deployments and documented the real request/response\ncontracts (not doc assumptions):\n\n- LLMPing v0.3.0: POST /chat {query, session_id} ->\n  {answer, provider, model}; GET /ping multi-provider probe;\n  session_id gives real server-side continuity; JSON requests\n  come back markdown-fenced (handled by _parse_json_reply)\n- WebHunter v1.1.0: POST /research/sync, async /research +\n  poll, POST /scrape; full response shapes captured\n- Live-verified behaviors: ~17-40% transient \"no search\n  results returned\" flakiness, frequently irrelevant results,\n  sync calls regularly 30-56s (at/over the 30s orchestrator\n  timeout), variants concatenated onto the base query\n- How the orchestrator consumes each response through the two\n  adapter clients, plus the discovery port mismatch (8765 vs\n  webhunter:8000)\n- Key finding: real LLMPing returns prose for full_analysis,\n  so bootstrap''s structured fields depend on LLMPing-side\n  structured output; the confidence/sourceCount gating in the\n  §5.1 lookup flow is validated against junk sources\n\nCo-authored-by: CommandCodeBot <noreply@commandcode.ai>","tree":{"sha":"56762300b4a16e5b754452ffe8c9cf1e857a3eaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nayaksomkar/CompetitorEngine/git/trees/56762300b4a16e5b754452ffe8c9cf1e857a3eaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nayaksomkar/CompetitorEngine/git/commits/618bcec64c70b5668731f059ad350421c16f81e6","verifica