4 definers x 4\ndeactivators, invariant: no cutoff names a non-ACTIVE path; red before the\nfix), lock-semantics integration tests, use-case unit tests.\n\n* docs: ADR 0028 and DDD pack - the path/CPT-schedule race is closed\n\nNew ADR 0028 (row-lock rule; ADR 0026 body untouched), ADR index entries\n(README, adr/about, sidebar), and the DDD pack: the eventstorming hotspot\nbecomes \"Decided 2026-10-06: closed (ADR 0028)\"; the deactivate and define\nsequence diagrams show FOR UPDATE / FOR SHARE; aggregate canvas, invariants\nand bounded-context canvas cite the lock.","tree":{"sha":"3929b4592f92e2a87a3234ea62ab92d2217e47c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/3929b4592f92e2a87a3234ea62ab92d2217e47c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/46b757f714cd369072e3e4f6aa43d0db3ce305d2","verification":{"payload":"tree 3929b4592f92e2a87a3234ea62ab92d2217e47c0\nparent 4a6083a39bc6a4906012d8206e8471a7ce70ff0d\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791329070 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791329070 -0300\n\nfix: close the path/CPT-schedule race with row locks (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#114)\n\n* fix: close the path/CPT-schedule race with row locks\n\nDefineCPTSchedule now locks every referenced path FOR SHARE (sorted,\ndeduped, one repository call) inside its unit of work before writing the\nschedule; DeactivatePath re-reads the path FOR UPDATE inside its unit of\nwork before looking for referencing schedules. Locking lives behind two new\nProcessPathRepo port methods (LockByIDsForShare, FindByIDForUpdate).\n\nTests: testcontainers race test (50 iterations x 4 definers x 4\ndeactivators, invariant: no cutoff names a non-ACTIVE path; red before the\nfix), lock-semantics integration tests, use-case unit tests.\n\n* docs: ADR 0028 and DDD pack - the path/CPT-schedule race is closed\n\nNew ADR 0028 (row-lock rule; ADR 0026 body untouched), ADR index entries