audioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/ece38e911fadc4f42743ff6e29114ba920a6712e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:21:26Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:21:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#111)\n\n* fix(http): reject null elements in request string arrays\n\nencoding/json turns a null element of a []string into \"\" without error,\nso {\"requiredCapabilities\":[\"pick\",null]} and the eligibility\nrequired/excludedProductAttributes arrays were accepted although the\npublished schema types every element as a non-null string. The\nSchemathesis contract job (stateful phase) caught this intermittently as\n\"API accepted schema-violating request ... was string, became null\",\ndepending on the generated seed.\n\nDecode those three arrays with a nonNullStrings type that returns an\nerror on a null element, so the handler answers 400 problem+json. Document\nthe 400 in apis/openapi.yaml and regenerate the REST API reference.\n\nReproduced with schemathesis 4.28.0 --seed 9; the new table test fails\nbefore and passes after.\n\n* fix(paths): insert-only DefinePath; refuse to deactivate scheduled paths\n\nItem: concurrent DefinePath of one id.\nDefinePath did FindByID and then Save, whose \"INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (id)\nDO UPDATE ... WHERE version = $11\" matched the winner''s row (a fresh\naggregate is also version 1), so a second concurrent define overwrote the\nfirst and both published ProcessPathCreated. Add the insert-only\nProcessPathRepo.Create (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING -> ports.ErrAlreadyExists)\nand make DefinePath use it, mapping the conflict to ErrPathAlreadyExists\n(409 path-already-exists). Integration test with testcontainers Postgres\nraces 8 defines of one id: exactly one wins, one outbox row; it failed on\nthe old upsert with concurrent-modification errors.\n\nItem: deactivating a path left CPT schedules naming it.\nADRs 0010/0001/0003 are silent, so pick reject-with-409 and record it in\nthe new ADR 0026: DeactivatePath asks the new\nCPTScheduleRepo.ListSiteIDsReferencingPath inside its unit of work and\nreturns ErrPathReferencedByCPTSchedule (409 path-referenced-by-cpt-schedule,\nnaming the sites) without mutating or publishing anything. Additive 409 on\nDELETE /process-paths/{pathId} documented in openapi.yaml; REST reference\nregenerated. Unit, BDD (2 scenarios) and Postgres integration tests added.\n\nDocs: sequence diagrams, aggregate design canvas, aggregates and\ninvariants, bounded context canvas and eventstorming updated; the two\nresolved hotspots removed and the residual concurrent-schedule race noted.\n\n* fix(events): propagate W3C trace context in Kafka headers; document omitted direct\n\napis/asyncapi.yaml promised traceparent/tracestate Kafka headers but\nPublisher.Send and the AnalyticsPublisher set only content-type.\n\n- The trace context is captured where the request span is still in ctx\n  (OutboxPublisher.Publish, and the direct/fan-out Publish paths) and\n  carried in Encoded.Trace; Publisher.Send writes it as headers. No\n  active span -> no trace headers; baggage is never propagated.\n- Outbox: migration 0008 adds nullable traceparent/tracestate columns\n  to outbox_events; the relay reads them back (the relay''s own context\n  has no relation to the request).\n- AsyncAPI: describe the trace headers precisely and document that\n  `direct: false` is omitted from the payload (omitempty).\n- New ADR 0027, index, sidebar, README, ddd pack (domain-events,\n  eventstorming hotspot removed, bounded-context-canvas open question\n  closed, entity-relationship).\n\nTests: unit tests for every publish path (direct, with-id, analytics,\nfan-out, relay Send, no-span) and a testcontainers integration test that\nthe trace context survives enqueue -> outbox row -> relay.\n\n* test(ci): harden the Kafka integration tests against slow runners\n\nFlaky CI on a docs-only PR: the analytics poison-message integration test\nfailed after 17s and three sibling tests then failed at 0s; the contract\njob reported \"API accepted schema-violating request\".\n\nContract job: the accepted schema-violating request was a JSON null inside\na string array (fixed in ce8682a); `make contract` now passes repeatedly\nacross random seeds. The \"schema validation mismatch ... mostly rejected\ngenerated data\" line is a Schemathesis WARNING that does not fail the job\n(the schema cannot express lower-case matchPrefix, positive durations or\nIANA zones, which the API enforces and tests elsewhere), so it is left as is.\n\nIntegration tests (no failing log survives for the superseded runs, so\nthese are the defects found by reading and timing the tests locally):\n- createTopic failed the test on the first dial/CreateTopics hiccup against\n  a freshly started broker -- and the broker is shared, so one hiccup\n  cascades to every later test as an instant failure. It now retries, and\n  waits for a partition LEADER (readable != writable) instead of metadata\n  only, which removes a multi-second publish retry loop.\n- Every test consumed in the production consumer group on the shared\n  broker; each test now uses its own group\n  (NewAnalyticsConsumerInGroup; NewAnalyticsConsumer is unchanged) and\n  cancels, waits for Run and Closes in t.Cleanup.\n- DLQ assertions used a consumer-group reader (extra coordinator\n  round-trip per test); they now read partition 0 directly.\n- Projection waits are 60s, not 30s: the work is sub-second, the budget is\n  dominated by the group join and must absorb a CPU-starved runner.","tree":{"sha":"004304ec338095a24f4d100f2d67a2a4cb0179d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/004304ec338095a24f4d100f2d67a2a4cb0179d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/ece38e911fadc4f42743ff6e29114ba920a6712e","verification":{"payload":"tree 004304ec338095a24f4d100f2d67a2a4cb0179d7\nparent e4239e77c6034fe20dad3b8177a6e9bb45d80aed\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791300086 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791300086 -0300\n\nfix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#111)\n\n* fix(http): reject null elements in request string arrays\n\nencoding/json turns a null element of a []string into \"\" without error,\nso {\"requiredCapabilities\":[\"pick\",null]} and the eligibility\nrequired/excludedProductAttributes arrays were accepted although the\npublished schema types every element as a non-null string. The\nSchemathesis contract job (stateful phase) caught this intermittently as\n\"API accepted schema-violating request ... was string, became null\",\ndepending on the generated seed.\n\nDecode those three arrays with a nonNullStrings type that returns an\nerror on a null element, so the handler answers 400 problem+json. Document\nthe 400 in apis/openapi.yaml and regenerate the REST API reference.\n\nReproduced with schemathesis 4.28.0 --seed 9; the new table test fails\nbefore and passes after.\n\n* fix(paths): insert-only DefinePath; refuse to deactivate scheduled paths\n\nItem: concurrent DefinePath of one id.\nDefinePath did FindByID and then Save, whose \"INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (id)\nDO UPDATE ... WHERE version = $11\" matched the winner''s row (a fresh\naggregate is also version 1), so a second concurrent define overwrote the\nfirst and both published ProcessPathCreated. Add the insert-only\nProcessPathRepo.Create (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING -> ports.ErrAlreadyExists)\nand make DefinePath use it, mapping the conflict to ErrPathAlreadyExists\n(409 path-already-exists). Integration test with testcontainers Postgres\nraces 8 defines of one id: exactly one wins, one outbox row; it failed on\nthe old upsert with concurrent-modification errors.\n\nItem: deactivating a path left CPT schedules naming it.\nADRs 0010/0001/0003 are silent, so pick reject-with-409 and record it in\nthe new ADR 0026: DeactivatePath asks the new\nCPTScheduleRepo.ListSiteIDsReferencingPath inside its unit of work and\nreturns ErrPathReferencedByCPTSchedule (409 path-referenced-by-cpt-schedule,\nnaming the sites) without mutating or publishing anything. Additive 409 on\nDELETE /process-paths/{pathId} documented in openapi.yaml; REST reference\nregenerated. Unit, BDD (2 scenarios) and Postgres integration tests added.\n\nDocs: sequence diagrams, aggregate design canvas, aggregates and\ninvariants, bounded context canvas and eventstorming updated; the two\nresolved hotspots removed and the residual concurrent-schedule race noted.\n\n* fix(events): propagate W3C trace context in Kafka headers; document omitted direct\n\napis/asyncapi.yaml promised traceparent/tracestate Kafka headers but\nPublisher.Send and the AnalyticsPublisher set only content-type.\n\n- The trace context is captured where the request span is still in ctx\n  (OutboxPublisher.Publish, and the direct/fan-out Publish paths) and\n  carried in Encoded.Trace; Publisher.Send writes it as headers. No\n  active span -> no trace headers; baggage is never propagated.\n- Outbox: migration 0008 adds nullable traceparent/tracestate columns\n  to outbox_events; the relay reads them back (the relay''s own context\n  has no relation to the request).\n- AsyncAPI: describe the trace headers precisely and document that\n  `direct: false` is omitted from the payload (omitempty).\n- New ADR 0027, index, sidebar, README, ddd pack (domain-events,\n  eventstorming hotspot removed, bounded-context-canvas open question\n  closed, entity-relationship).\n\nTests: unit tests for every publish path (direct, with-id, analytics,\nfan-out, relay Send, no-span) and a testcontainers integration test that\nthe trace context survives enqueue -> outbox row -> relay.\n\n* test(ci): harden the Kafka integration tests against slow runners\n\nFlaky CI on a docs-only PR: the analytics poison-message integration test\nfailed after 17s and three sibling tests then failed at 0s; the contract\njob reported \"API accepted schema-violating request\".\n\nContract job: the accepted schema-violating request was a JSON null inside\na string array (fixed in ce8682a); `make contract` now passes repeatedly\nacross random seeds. The \"schema validation mismatch ... mostly rejected\ngenerated data\" line is a Schemathesis WARNING that does not fail the job\n(the schema cannot express lower-case matchPrefix, positive durations or\nIANA zones, which the API enforces and tests elsewhere), so it is left as is.\n\nIntegration tests (no failing log survives for the superseded runs, so\nthese are the defects found by reading and timing the tests locally):\n- createTopic failed the test on the first dial/CreateTopics hiccup against\n  a freshly started broker -- and the broker is shared, so one hiccup\n  cascades to every later test as an instant failure. It now retries, and\n  waits for a partition LEADER (readable != writable) instead of metadata\n  only, which removes a multi-second publish retry loop.\n- Every test consumed in the production consumer group on the shared\n  broker; each test now uses its own group\n  (NewAnalyticsConsumerInGroup; NewAnalyticsConsumer is unchanged) and\n  cancels, waits for Run and Closes in t.Cleanup.\n- DLQ assertions used a consumer-group reader (extra coordinator\n  round-trip per test); they now read partition 0 directly.\n- Projection waits are 60s, not 30s: the work is sub-second, the budget is\n  dominated by the group join and must absorb a CPU-starved runner.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxRH2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWTsQABWpGhDDQThq3UUXrOMdc2s4\n1cYmF5y1kMT4W7C/gXcm/itCYrrflbJZDmQ+6nR7tbStb3eivBj1c+jrypjoAeJy\nsn11hOHGUXA687PaLOV7nUtnRXA4VhiakYU36HhfgEZtGVszpQoz1Aleke8z/kUm\nQoSKVnGmZUxqU8PTv6iq0ObXvbLw5veHwh8wkQT4p4UPWpw65+yzwYHDHNoCR3pM\n17AYIt56UtGa/S54hWjtwZz7K31851EG6f8zduaYDyDxT7ecabT7S/YtxSrrehvF\npVTxcuiDutUnpSM8pnH+mJLBip3KWWq6Y0Krhp4hRmNpY61x53KGQ8e6eztuLu4e\nG+4n87s4IfW/MYTgrIcsw45QCXrzDZOm4XtsIab+lig0GUfPXAV+uK81tD8wuc/l\n6JUf5nl1ghS5Os9VVTLNUV6XUzES0WJciD/WtxhqQRGQJISrwqLLqxXrKNAhYpAq\nLZ5xTKHjgEtRxtfgHWlNkDS5HStD2nKE29e+l1cpt+djuyrl4mSPYDKQ6AqJ8k4n\njzzmU+o6AqYP2UPw2Vn1HRzug/hBYTA34UiUCPWLuo5ckAZIxZLedLlkIbSstxqj\n+4exRdqEYxWUCKANznbOK7urCQnswA37DKJTodARMcHSAPJe9heCiiRcgMaKGIDc\nWoUSBsFJ1pDglmjeJHx6\n=NKAC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T15:21:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com