DQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/95c6e56e62c082ef8082d7a9ab405fa3727891bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:53:31Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:53:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#108)\n\n* docs: refresh README and agent rules against develop\n\n- README: IQVO docs URL, migrations 0001-0007, /readyz route, missing\n  env vars (MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, HOUSEKEEPING_INTERVAL,\n  IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_TTL, OUTBOX_RETENTION, SERVICE_VERSION, ENVIRONMENT),\n  Idempotency-Key only enforced with DATABASE_URL, testcontainers-based\n  integration, 30 BDD scenarios, full CI job list, network-fulfillment\n  consumer, refreshed known gaps, full ADR list 0001-0025.\n- SECURITY.md: IQVO advisory link.\n- .claude/rules: readyz, BDD feature list, testcontainers, CI jobs,\n  migration range, network-fulfillment as fifth consumer.\n\n* docs: WIP DDD artifact pack (agent interrupted by rate limit)\n\nPartial, unverified work committed to preserve it; the resume run reviews,\ncompletes and validates it.\n\n* docs(ddd): verify WIP DDD pages against code\n\nCorrect claims in the WIP artifact pages that the code does not support:\nconsumer-side deactivation behaviour is now described as each consumer''s\napplyDeactivated handler, the CPT eligibility check is a note rather than\na fake self-query, the MCP report tool is shown as cmd/mcp forwarding to\npathmgmt-reports, Eligibility is no longer called a value type with\nrules, and the analytics DLQ also covers projection failures after the\nbounded retries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ddd): complete the ddd-crew artifact pack and wire the sidebar\n\nAdd the index page, EventStorming boards, UML class diagrams, ER diagrams\nof both databases and sequence diagrams for every command use case, all\nderived from the code. Wire the whole pack into a \"DDD artifacts\n(ddd-crew)\" sidebar category, with the existing context map inside it.\nFix the fan-out publisher type name on the domain events page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(context-map): order-management is Generic/Supporting, not Core\n\nMatches order-management''s own subdomain classification page and the\nfleet aggregator.\n\n* docs(claude): network-fulfillment is also a Conformist consumer\n\n* docs: order-management is Generic/Supporting in the consumer table too\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b716da9dcaf98f1311241a3e1689c87eb905027","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/0b716da9dcaf98f1311241a3e1689c87eb905027"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/95c6e56e62c082ef8082d7a9ab405fa3727891bd","verification":{"payload":"tree 0b716da9dcaf98f1311241a3e1689c87eb905027\nparent ffc7ab859e5df1eaba402a9d9af52cdc025dca1a\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791269611 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791269611 -0300\n\ndocs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#108)\n\n* docs: refresh README and agent rules against develop\n\n- README: IQVO docs URL, migrations 0001-0007, /readyz route, missing\n  env vars (MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, HOUSEKEEPING_INTERVAL,\n  IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_TTL, OUTBOX_RETENTION, SERVICE_VERSION, ENVIRONMENT),\n  Idempotency-Key only enforced with DATABASE_URL, testcontainers-based\n  integration, 30 BDD scenarios, full CI job list, network-fulfillment\n  consumer, refreshed known gaps, full ADR list 0001-0025.\n- SECURITY.md: IQVO advisory link.\n- .claude/rules: readyz, BDD feature list, testcontainers, CI jobs,\n  migration range, network-fulfillment as fifth consumer.\n\n* docs: WIP DDD artifact pack (agent interrupted by rate limit)\n\nPartial, unverified work committed to preserve it; the resume run reviews,\ncompletes and validates it.\n\n* docs(ddd): verify WIP DDD pages against code\n\nCorrect claims in the WIP artifact pages that the code does not support:\nconsumer-side deactivation behaviour is now described as each consumer''s\napplyDeactivated handler, the CPT eligibility check is a note rather than\na fake self-query, the MCP report tool is shown as cmd/mcp forwarding to\npathmgmt-reports, Eligibility is no longer called a value type with\nrules, and the analytics DLQ also covers projection failures after the\nbounded retries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ddd): complete the ddd-crew artifact pack and wire the sidebar\n\nAdd the index page, EventStorming boards, UML class diagrams, ER diagrams\nof both databases and sequence diagrams for every command use case, all\nderived from the code. Wire the whole pack into a \"DDD artifacts\n(ddd-crew)\" sidebar category, with the existing context map inside it.\nFix the fan-out publisher type name on the domain events page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(context-map): order-management is Generic/Supporting, not Core\n\nMatches order-management''s own subdomain classification page and the\nfleet aggregator.\n\n* docs(claude): network-fulfillment is also a Conformist consumer\n\n* docs: order-management is Generic/Supporting in the consumer table too\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude 