.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/1279cb6044811cf6074e8df2d503080cf98d890c","node_id":"C_kwDOUPuTL9oAKDEyNzljYjYwNDQ4MTFjZjYwNzRlOGRmMmQ1MDMwODBjZjk4ZDg5MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/a65eeda299e3bd70677ba4c00f8ceb11e47a93e0","sha":"a65eeda299e3bd70677ba4c00f8ceb11e47a93e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/a65eeda299e3bd70677ba4c00f8ceb11e47a93e0"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/1794ed4c3706e4f8a788bc4702c7ca7e4ac0f9c6","sha":"1794ed4c3706e4f8a788bc4702c7ca7e4ac0f9c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/1794ed4c3706e4f8a788bc4702c7ca7e4ac0f9c6"}],"sha":"1279cb6044811cf6074e8df2d503080cf98d890c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/1279cb6044811cf6074e8df2d503080cf98d890c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/1794ed4c3706e4f8a788bc4702c7ca7e4ac0f9c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T10:06:13Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T10:06:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: ADR-conformance gaps (2026-10-04 audit) + OCC rollout (#100)\n\n* fix(kafka): share one CloudEvents id per occurrence on the direct fan-out path\n\nADR 0016 dev-only edge: with EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka and no Postgres, each\npublisher minted its own id, so the integration and analytics topics\ndisagreed about the same occurrence''s id. NewSharedIdFanOut now mints\nONE id per occurrence and publishes under it on both topics via the new\nPublisher.PublishWithId / AnalyticsPublisher.PublishWithId seams,\nmatching postgres.OutboxPublisher semantics. ADR 0016 gains a note.\n\n* fix(mcp): share ONE OLTP pool across both repos (ADR 0014 arithmetic)\n\ncmd/mcp opened two MaxConns=10 pools (buildRepo + buildCPTScheduleRepo),\nso a pod could hold 20 connections against ADR 0014''s 10-per-pod budget.\nbuildRepo now returns its already-pinged pool and\nbuildCPTScheduleRepo reuses it — the same single-pool shape\ncmd/pathmgmt/buildPersistence uses for the same two repos. ADR 0014\ngains a note; TestBuildCPTScheduleRepo_SharesBuildRepoPool pins the\nwiring; TestNewPool_AppliesMaxConns still asserts 10.\n\n* fix(mfe,api): ADR-0010 capability fields on the MFE + ADR-0011 Idempotency-Key adoption\n\nItem 1 (ADR-0010): the MFE''s types and forms lacked cycleTimeP95 and\neligibility, so every define/revise POST/PUT was rejected 422\n(parseCycleTimeP95(\"\") -> ErrInvalidCycleTime). Both forms now carry\nthem (2h default, permissive eligibility by default), and the list shows\ncycleTimeP95, eligibility and destinationLocationRole. The MCP\nlist/get DTO also gains destinationLocationRole (omitempty when unset),\nwhich the REST wire always carried.\n\nItem 3 (ADR-0011): apis/openapi.yaml documents the Idempotency-Key\nheader on POST /process-paths (required: false, no minLength; the\ndescription mandates a non-empty key; 400 idempotency-key-required and\n422 idempotency-key-reused noted). CORS AllowedHeaders now permits\nIdempotency-Key with a preflight test. web api.ts mints a per-submit\ncrypto.randomUUID() key on every POST so the console no longer 400s\nagainst a Postgres-backed deployment.\n\n* docs(api): regenerate REST API docs for the Idempotency-Key header\n\nclean-api-docs + gen-api-docs per the fleet rule (generator caches);\ndocs build passes.\n\n* test(arch): scan inbound adapters for sibling-context HTTP clients + doc drift fixes\n\nItem 5: TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls now walks BOTH\ninternal/adapters/outbound and internal/adapters/inbound, matching\nHTTP-client constructs (*http.Client, http.NewRequest*, ...) rather\nthan the bare net/http import, with an explicit same-context allowlist\n(report_tool.go -> pathmgmt-reports, ADR 0007 §4). A violation-fixture\ntest proves the detector fires and that server-only net/http use is not\nflagged.\n\nItem 4 (part): about.md annotates 0003''s index row (superseded-by-0016\nstored format); ADR-0001 + values.yaml drop the stale ''no consumer\nwired yet''; ADR-0004/0005 fix ''no MCP adapter / no reports binary'';\ndto.go + publisher.go cite ADR 0009 (not 0006) for\ndestinationLocationRole; ADR-0010 fixes the migration name\n(0005_capability), the flat 2h backfill story, and the list_process_paths\ntool name; ADR-0014 fixes the fitness-test file path; ADR-0015 fixes the\nHPA value key (autoscaling.api.enabled).\n\n* style: gofmt fanout_publisher_test.go\n\n* feat(occ): optimistic concurrency on ProcessPath and CPTSchedule (ADR 0017)\n\n- version column on process_paths + cpt_schedules (migration 0007)\n- version-guarded upserts in both Postgres repos; RowsAffected==0 ->\n  ports.ErrConcurrentModification\n- Rehydrate carries the row''s version; Define starts at 1\n- HTTP maps it to 409 with its own concurrent-modification RFC 7807\n  category, distinct from path-already-exists\n- OpenAPI: 409 on both mutating PUTs + regenerated API docs\n- testcontainers race tests: stale save rejected, exactly one winner,\n  exactly one version increment, for both aggregates\n\n* feat(ops): outbox lag gauge + housekeeping sweeper (ADR 0018)\n\n- process_path_management.outbox.lag_seconds async gauge behind the\n  relay, closing ADR 0003''s deferred follow-up\n- Sweeper bounds idempotency_keys (24h TTL) and published outbox_events\n  (7d retention); unpublished rows never swept; batched DELETEs\n- envs HOUSEKEEPING_INTERVAL / IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_TTL / OUTBOX_RETENTION\n  read in cmd/pathmgmt, wired into the chart under config.housekeeping\n- testcontainers tests for sweep semantics + lag query semantics\n\n* docs(adr): adoption records for undocumented features (0019-0025)\n\n- 0019 standard metrics convention (also fixes the phantom\n  ''fleet-standard-metrics ADR'' citations in metrics.go, ports.go,\n  server.go)\n- 0020 RFC 7807 problem details\n- 0021 architecture fitness suite\n- 0022 MFE console remote (+ the ADR 0010 capability-fields lesson)\n- 0023 MCP eval & governance harness\n- 0024 bootretry for Istio native-sidecar warm-up\n- 0025 Schemathesis contract job\nAll added to about.md index + sidebars.ts; docs build passes.\n\n* test(integration): migrate remaining Postgres tests off env-gated skips\n\nConvert analyticsstore and postgres package integration tests that still\nrequired ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL/DATABASE_URL (t.Skip when unset) to\ntestcontainers-go, matching the fleet rule: Postgres/Kafka integration\ntests must self-provision, never env-gated skip. Verified against real\nDocker containers (all pass).","tree":{"sha":"968491075cf73951189b149b692e7c597e7139a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/968491075cf73951189b149b692e7c597e7139a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/1794ed4c3706e4f8a788bc4702c7ca7e4ac0f9c6","verification":{"payload":"tree 968491075cf73951189b149b692e7c597e7139a1\nparent 419940c0156c08cbb3860fe2c68e075a6f7cd752\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791194773 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791194773 -0300\n\nfix: ADR-conformance gaps (2026-10-04 audit) + OCC rollout (#100)\n\n* fix(kafka): share one CloudEvents id per occurrence on the direct fan-out path\n\nADR 0016 dev-only edge: with EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka and no Postgres, each\npublisher minted its own id, so the integration and analytics topics\ndisagreed about the same occurrence''s id. NewSharedIdFanOut now mints\nONE id per occurrence and publishes under it on both topics via the new\nPublisher.PublishWithId / AnalyticsPublisher.PublishWithId seams,\nmatching postgres.OutboxPublisher semantics. ADR 0016 gains a note.\n\n* fix(mcp): share ONE OLTP pool across both repos (ADR 0014 arithmetic)\n\ncmd/mcp opened two MaxConns=10 pools (buildRepo + buildCPTScheduleRepo),\nso a pod could hold 20 connections against ADR 0014''s 10-per-pod budget.\nbuildRepo now returns its already-pinged pool and\nbuildCPTScheduleRepo reuses it — the same single-pool shape\ncmd/pathmgmt/buildPersistence uses for the same two repos. ADR 0014\ngains a note; TestBuildCPTScheduleRepo_SharesBuildRepoPool pins the\nwiring; TestNewPool_AppliesMaxConns still asserts 10.\n\n* fix(mfe,api): ADR-0010 capability fields on the MFE + ADR-0011 Idempotency-Key adoption\n\nItem 1 (ADR-0010): the MFE''s types and forms lacked cycleTimeP95 and\neligibility, so every define/revise POST/PUT was rejected 422\n(parseCycleTimeP95(\"\") -> ErrInvalidCycleTime). Both forms now carry\nthem (2h default, permissive eligibility by default), and the list shows\ncycleTimeP95, eligibility and destinationLocationRole. The MCP\nlist/get DTO also gains destinationLocationRole (omitempty when unset),\nwhich the REST wire always carried.\n\nItem 3 (ADR-0011): apis/openapi.yaml documents the Idempotency-Key\nheader on POST /process-paths (required: false, no minLength; the\ndescription mandates a non-empty key; 400 idempotency-key-required and\n422 idempotency-key-reused noted). CORS AllowedHeaders now permits\nIdempotency-Key with a preflight test. web api.ts mints a per-submit\ncrypto.randomUUID() key on every POST so the console no longer 400s\nagainst a Postgres-backed deployment.\n\n* docs(api): regenerate REST API docs for the Idempotency-Key header\n\nclean-api-docs + gen-api-docs per the fleet rule (generator caches);\ndocs build passes.\n\n* test(arch): scan inbound adapters for sibling-context HTTP clients + doc drift fixes\n\nItem 5: TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls now walks BOTH\ninternal/adapters/outbound and internal/adapters/inbound, matching\nHTTP-client constructs (*http.Client, http.NewRequest*, ...) rather\nthan the bare net/http import, with an explicit same-context allowlist\n(report_tool.go -> pathmgmt-reports, ADR 0007 §4). A violation-fixture\ntest proves the detector fires and that server-only net/http use is not\nflagged.\n\nItem 4 (part): about.md annotates 0003''s index row (superseded-by-0016\nstored format); ADR-0001 + values.yaml drop the stale ''no consumer\nwired yet''; ADR-0004/0005 fix ''no MCP adapter / no reports binary'';\ndto.go + publisher.go cite ADR 0009 (not 0006) for\ndestinationLocationRole; ADR-0010 fixes the migration name\n(0005_capability), the flat 2h backfill story, and the list_process_paths\ntool name; ADR-0014 fixes the fitness-test file path; ADR-0015 fixes the\nHPA value key (autoscaling.api.enabled).\n\n* style: gofmt fanout_publisher_test.go\n\n* feat(occ): optimistic concurrency on ProcessPath and CPTSchedule (ADR 0017)\n\n- version column on process_paths + cpt_schedules (migration 0007)\n- version-guarded upserts in both Postgres repos; RowsAffected==0 ->\n  ports.ErrConcurrentModification\n- Rehydrate carries the row''s version; Define starts at 1\n- HTTP maps it to 409 with its own concurrent-modification RFC 7807\n  category, distinct from path-already-exists\n- OpenAPI: 409 on both mutating PUTs + regenerated API docs\n- testcontainers race tests: stale save rejected, exactly one winner,\n  exactly one version increment, for both aggregates\n\n* feat(ops): outbox lag gauge + housekeeping sweeper (ADR 0018)\n\n- process_path_management.outbox.lag_seconds async gauge behind the\n  relay, closing ADR 0003''s deferred follow-up\n- Sweeper bounds idempotency_keys (24h TTL) and published outbox_events\n  (7d retention); unpublished rows never swept; batched DELETEs\n- envs HOUSEKEEPING_INTERVAL / IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_TTL / OUTBOX_RETENTION\n  read in cmd/pathmgmt, wired into the chart under config.housekeeping\n- testcontainers tests for sweep semantics + lag query semantics\n\n* docs(adr): adoption records for undocumented features (0019-0025)\n\n- 0019 standard metrics convention (also fixes the phantom\n  ''fleet-standard-metrics ADR'' citations in metrics.go, ports.go,\n  server.go)\n- 0020 RFC 7807 problem details\n- 0021 architecture fitness suite\n- 0022 MFE console remote (+ the ADR 0010 capability-fields lesson)\n- 0023 MCP eval & governance harness\n- 0024 bootretry for Istio native-sidecar warm-up\n- 0025 Schemathesis contract job\nAll added to about.md index + sidebars.ts; docs build passes.\n\n* test(integration): migrate remaining Postgres tests off env-gated skips\n\nConvert analyticsstore and postgres package integration tests that still\nrequired ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL/DATABASE_URL (t.Skip when unset) to\ntestcontainers-go, matching the fleet rule: Postgres/Kafka integration\ntests must self-provision, never env-gated skip. Verified against real\nDocker containers (all pass).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw3aVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUFkQA