tion":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/2dff8b43cce59d38f7b4307957700491d1198ad0","node_id":"C_kwDOUPuTL9oAKDJkZmY4YjQzY2NlNTlkMzhmN2I0MzA3OTU3NzAwNDkxZDExOThhZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/82401206479275384287034af471af524cb4e0a3","sha":"82401206479275384287034af471af524cb4e0a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/82401206479275384287034af471af524cb4e0a3"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/9da0cad779af4114c99a271a6e4af12786575e6e","sha":"9da0cad779af4114c99a271a6e4af12786575e6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/9da0cad779af4114c99a271a6e4af12786575e6e"}],"sha":"2dff8b43cce59d38f7b4307957700491d1198ad0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/2dff8b43cce59d38f7b4307957700491d1198ad0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/82401206479275384287034af471af524cb4e0a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:22:18Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:22:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#80)\n\nFleet-wide fix, ported from order-management''s ADR-0029 (PR #115),\nthis repo''s own AGENTS.md-verified reference implementation.\ngolang-migrate''s postgres driver takes a session-scoped\npg_advisory_lock to serialize concurrent migration runs, but\nDATABASE_URL (warehouse-infra PR #43, PgBouncer rollout) points this\nservice''s OLTP database at PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode,\nwhich does not preserve session state across statements. Two or more\nreplicas of cmd/pathmgmt or cmd/mcp starting concurrently (an HPA\nscale-out, or an ordinary rolling deploy with replicas>1) would\ncrash-loop with ''pq: unnamed prepared statement does not exist'' /\n''pq: canceling statement due to statement timeout'' for ~1-2 minutes\nuntil one wins the advisory-lock race.\n\ncmd/pathmgmt/main.go and cmd/mcp/main.go (both run migrations at\nstartup) now read a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var for the\nmigration step only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset:\n\n    migrationsDatabaseURL := getenv(\"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\", databaseURL)\n\nThe pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses\ndatabaseURL unchanged — every request either binary serves keeps\ngoing through PgBouncer exactly as before. The fallback keeps local\ndev and CI integration tests working byte-identically to before this\nchange.\n\ncmd/pathmgmt-projector and cmd/pathmgmt-reports are unaffected: they\nrun against ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL, this service''s own analytical\ndatabase, which was never routed through PgBouncer.\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #44 already provisions MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL as\na secret key for all 9 OLTP services, this one included — no\nwarehouse-infra changes needed.\n\nAdds:\n- TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback (cmd/pathmgmt, cmd/mcp): proves\n  the getenv fallback in both directions.\n- TestBuildPersistence_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations\n  / TestBuildRepo_...: prove buildPersistence/buildRepo thread\n  migrationsDatabaseURL into the migration step, not databaseURL.\n- ADR 0015: documents the pg_advisory_lock / transaction-pooling\n  incompatibility, cross-references order-management''s ADR-0029 and\n  warehouse-infra PR #43/#44.\n- charts/process-path-management: a new\n  database.migrationsExistingSecretKey value (default\n  \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders a MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env\n  var, sourced from the same existingSecret, in both the api and mcp\n  Deployments (optional: true on the secretKeyRef so a secret that\n  predates this key still starts the pod).\n\nhelm lint and helm template ... | grep MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL both\nverified locally. make check, make check-all (coverage 99.7%, gate\n90%; 30/30 BDD scenarios; arch-test) and make integration all pass.","tree":{"sha":"27b964ce62843d5ecda5ae02e6369429d96012e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/27b964ce62843d5ecda5ae02e6369429d96012e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/82401206479275384287034af471af524cb4e0a3","verification":{"payload":"tree 27b964ce62843d5ecda5ae02e6369429d96012e6\nparent 92d62513c0c03b9b453360c91f526846ef324f07\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790601738 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790601738 -0300\n\nfix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#80)\n\nFleet-wide fix, ported from order-management''s ADR-0029 (PR #115),\nthis repo''s own AGENTS.md-verified reference implementation.\ngolang-migrate''s postgres driver takes a session-scoped\npg_advisory_lock to serialize concurrent migration runs, but\nDATABASE_URL (warehouse-infra PR #43, PgBouncer rollout) points this\nservice''s OLTP database at PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode,\nwhich does not preserve session state across statements. Two or more\nreplicas of cmd/pathmgmt or cmd/mcp starting concurrently (an HPA\nscale-out, or an ordinary rolling deploy with replicas>1) would\ncrash-loop with ''pq: unnamed prepared statement does not exist'' /\n''pq: canceling statement due to statement timeout'' for ~1-2 minutes\nuntil one wins the advisory-lock race.\n\ncmd/pathmgmt/main.go and cmd/mcp/main.go (both run migrations at\nstartup) now read a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env var for the\nmigration step only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when unset:\n\n    migrationsDatabaseURL := getenv(\"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\", databaseURL)\n\nThe pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses\ndatabaseURL unchanged — every request either binary serves keeps\ngoing through PgBouncer exactly as before. The fallback keeps local\ndev and CI integration tests working byte-identically to before this\nchange.\n\ncmd/pathmgmt-projector and cmd/pathmgmt-reports are unaffected: they\nrun against ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL, this service''s own analytical\ndatabase, which was never routed through PgBouncer.\n\nwarehouse-infra PR #44 already provisions MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL as\na secret key for all 9 OLTP services, this one included — no\nwarehouse-infra changes needed.\n\nAdds:\n- TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback (cmd/pathmgmt, cmd/mcp): proves\n  the getenv fallback in both directions.\n- TestBuildPersistence_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations\n  / TestBuildRepo_...: prove buildPersistence/buildRepo thread\n  migrationsDatabaseURL into the migration step, not databaseURL.\n- ADR 0015: documents the pg_advisory_lock / transaction-pooling\n  incompatibility, cross-references order-management''s ADR-0029 and\n  warehouse-infra PR #43/#44.\n- charts/process-path-management: a new\n  database.migrationsExistingSecretKey value (default\n  \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders a MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL env\n  var, sourced from the same existingSecret, in both the api and mcp\n  Deployments (optional: true on the secretKeyRef so a secret that\n  predates this key still starts the pod).\n\nhelm lint and helm template ... | grep MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL both\nverified locally. make check, make check-all (coverage 99.7%, gate\n90%; 30/30 BDD scenarios; arch-test) and make integration all pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumoKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALewQAJpIII16V31ESR1wmCXtIHXI\nMwzRzrQKv19tLbYACUe/GeBV68d8gF68RvyZ2yw8z2/qO0OOjz4nUY3jka33Hp3G\nVV5xNkHctEuuPpLWWnKJ5Ikp8uJeNrcqDgQ0SzPs6G/P+1psaL5bWeSdz5vTpu7v\nWSK5EPAAgXcLjbI85VTzrs1n+wVkV52uD+j48e1DFRuUkZY0rTrnQbTILwD6bqSV\nFJpPmfTtBITAdpng8hufg6mZ8FwLecwBLJLzNt+A+s1IMp+hqsoc7PxwQekSZ+xo\n/snDkE6Uo47v0ICpkEjUxUiaXQeSP/PR3S8T7Az0j77MHnMYEgpsdif23q8f+t16\n6zYrnF773EjhJZcbeSnUYl1N3Pn2t2sBEq8aZXFxU3a