organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/0603aa8932d276a86693169b90af3112444b5c93","node_id":"C_kwDOUPuTL9oAKDA2MDNhYTg5MzJkMjc2YTg2NjkzMTY5YjkwYWYzMTEyNDQ0YjVjOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/2d17ff8e594dc831915e37f436100dd993a36ffd","sha":"2d17ff8e594dc831915e37f436100dd993a36ffd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/2d17ff8e594dc831915e37f436100dd993a36ffd"}],"sha":"0603aa8932d276a86693169b90af3112444b5c93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/0603aa8932d276a86693169b90af3112444b5c93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/2d17ff8e594dc831915e37f436100dd993a36ffd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:56Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:59:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0014) (#79)\n\nPhase 3 (scalability) of the fleet production-readiness plan, porting\norder-management''s ADR 0026 / PR #110 (the fleet''s Phase 3 reference)\nonto process-path-management''s own binary shape.\n\nHorizontalPodAutoscaler (autoscaling/v2), one per independently\nassessed Deployment:\n\n- api: min 1 / max 4 / target 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP HTTP with NO\n  inbound Kafka consumer at all (this service is the published-language\n  SOURCE, never a consumer). Its only background work, the in-process\n  OutboxRelay, claims rows via SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED,\n  already documented safe for concurrent instances.\n- analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 / target 70% CPU (capped below\n  api''s 4). Its AnalyticsConsumerGroup is a stable shared Kafka group,\n  verified in internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/analytics_consumer.go, so\n  N replicas share partitions safely, but wider fan-out buys little for\n  a lightweight idempotent-upsert projection workload.\n- analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / target 70% CPU. Stateless\n  read-only REST reader, same treatment as api.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / target 70% CPU. Pure static-asset serving,\n  no server-side state.\n- mcp: deliberately NO autoscaling block at all (not just disabled).\n  The MCP Go SDK''s StreamableHTTPHandler keeps in-memory session state\n  keyed by Mcp-Session-Id with no sticky routing configured on\n  mcp-service.yaml; >1 replica can misroute a mid-session request.\n  Documented in values.yaml and ADR 0014.\n\nEvery autoscaling.<component>.enabled defaults to false in values.yaml\nso this PR changes no production replica behavior on merge. Each\nDeployment template guards its replicas: field with\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so a hardcoded replica\ncount never fights an active HPA controller — verified with\nhelm template across default (0 HPAs), all-enabled (4 HPAs, mcp none),\nand mixed-enablement (only the matching Deployment loses replicas:)\ncombinations.\n\npgxpool tuning: explicit MaxConns matching order-management''s numbers,\nreplacing the CPU-derived library default (max(4, NumCPU())):\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.NewPool, cmd/pathmgmt + cmd/mcp): MaxConns=10.\n  This service''s OLTP DATABASE_URL is already re-pointed at PgBouncer\n  (warehouse-infra PR #43), so this is a PgBouncer-side client ceiling,\n  not a 1:1 server-side connection count.\n- Analytics writer pool (analyticsstore.NewPool, cmd/pathmgmt-projector):\n  MaxConns=5. Direct-to-Postgres (analytics DSNs stay outside PgBouncer\n  per PR #43''s own split), capped at HPA max 2 replicas.\n- Analytics reader pool (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool,\n  cmd/pathmgmt-reports): MaxConns=5. Direct-to-Postgres, HPA max 3\n  replicas.\n\nstatement_timeout via pgxpool.Config.AfterConnect (SET on every new\nconnection, not per-query), matching order-management''s values:\nOLTP 5s, analytics writer 10s, analytics reader 15s.\n\nNew internal/adapters/outbound/postgres/pool_limits_integration_test.go\nproves both settings against a real testcontainers Postgres: a real\npg_sleep is confirmed cancelled by Postgres at the configured\nstatement_timeout (SQLSTATE 57014); MaxConns is proven to actually\nblock a further Acquire once exhausted.\n\nADR 0014 documents both halves, referencing order-management''s ADR\n0026 and warehouse-infra PR #43''s PgBouncer split, including the\nservice''s own connection-budget accounting (narrower than\norder-management''s pre-PgBouncer accounting, since the OLTP path now\nruns through PgBouncer) as a documented residual risk, not a solved\none.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + integration), gofmt clean, make check\n(fmt-check/vet/build/lint/test -race, 0 lint issues), make arch-test\n(all hexagonal + fleet-specific fitness tests pass, including\nTestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls), go test -tags=integration ./...\n-race -count=1 (all packages pass, including the new pool-limits\ntests against real testcontainers Postgres), make coverage (99.7%,\ngate 90%), helm lint, helm template smoke render (default/all-enabled/\nmixed).","tree":{"sha":"96b05ca47003eb53c696d79a8e3e860f1cf42c32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/96b05ca47003eb53c696d79a8e3e860f1cf42c32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/2d17ff8e594dc831915e37f436100dd993a36ffd","verification":{"payload":"tree 96b05ca47003eb53c696d79a8e3e860f1cf42c32\nparent 2474238e7c044ac963c552bf5df241f334e2b588\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790567996 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790567996 -0300\n\nfeat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (ADR 0014) (#79)\n\nPhase 3 (scalability) of the fleet production-readiness plan, porting\norder-management''s ADR 0026 / PR #110 (the fleet''s Phase 3 reference)\nonto process-path-management''s own binary shape.\n\nHorizontalPodAutoscaler (autoscaling/v2), one per independently\nassessed Deployment:\n\n- api: min 1 / max 4 / target 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP HTTP with NO\n  inbound Kafka consumer at all (this service is the published-language\n  SOURCE, never a consumer). Its only background work, the in-process\n  OutboxRelay, claims rows via SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED,\n  already documented safe for concurrent instances.\n- analytics-projector: min 1 / max 2 / target 70% CPU (capped below\n  api''s 4). Its AnalyticsConsumerGroup is a stable shared Kafka group,\n  verified in internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/analytics_consumer.go, so\n  N replicas share partitions safely, but wider fan-out buys little for\n  a lightweight idempotent-upsert projection workload.\n- analytics-reports: min 1 / max 3 / target 70% CPU. Stateless\n  read-only REST reader, same treatment as api.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / target 70% CPU. Pure static-asset serving,\n  no server-side state.\n- mcp: deliberately NO autoscaling block at all (not just disabled).\n  The MCP Go SDK''s StreamableHTTPHandler keeps in-memory session state\n  keyed by Mcp-Session-Id with no sticky routing configured on\n  mcp-service.yaml; >1 replica can misroute a mid-session request.\n  Documented in values.yaml and ADR 0014.\n\nEvery autoscaling.<component>.enabled defaults to false in values.yaml\nso this PR changes no production replica behavior on merge. Each\nDeployment template guards its replicas: field with\n`{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so a hardcoded replica\ncount never fights an active HPA controller — verified with\nhelm template across default (0 HPAs), all-enabled (4 HPAs, mcp none),\nand mixed-enablement (only the matching Deployment loses replicas:)\ncombinations.\n\npgxpool tuning: explicit MaxConns matching order-management''s numbers,\nreplacing the CPU-derived library default (max(4, NumCPU())):\n\n- OLTP pool (postgres.NewPool, cmd/pathmgmt + cmd/mcp): MaxConns=10.\n  This service''s OLTP DATABASE_URL is already re-pointed at PgBouncer\n  (warehouse-infra PR #43), so this is a PgBouncer-side client ceiling,\n  not a 1:1 server-side connection count.\n- Analytics writer pool (analyticsstore.NewPool, cmd/pathmgmt-projector):\n  MaxConns=5. Direct-to-Postgres (analytics DSNs stay outside PgBouncer\n  per PR #43''s own split), capped at HPA max 2 replicas.\n- Analytics reader pool (analyticsstore.NewReadOnlyPool,\n  cmd/pathmgmt-reports): MaxConns=5. Direct-to-Postgres, HPA max 3\n  replicas.\n\nstatement_timeout via pgxpool.Config.AfterConnect (SET on every new\nconnection, not per-query), matching order-management''s values:\nOLTP 5s, analytics writer 10s, analytics reader 15s.\n\nNew internal/adapters/outbound/postgres/pool_limits_integration_test.go\nproves both settings against a real testcontainers Postgres: a real\npg_sleep is confirmed cancelled by Postgres at the configured\nstatement_timeout (SQLSTATE 57014); MaxConns is proven to actually\nblock a further Acquire once exhausted.\n\nADR 0014 documents both halves, referencing order-management''s ADR\n0026 and warehouse-infra PR #43''s PgBouncer split, including the\nservice''s own connection-budget accounting (narrower than\norder-management''s pre-PgBouncer accounting, since the OLTP path now\nruns through PgBouncer) as a documented residual risk, not a solved\none.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + integration), gofmt clean, make check\n(fmt-check/vet/build/lint/test -race, 0 lint issues), make arch-test\n(all hexagonal + fleet-specific fitness tests pass, including\nTestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls), go test -tags=integration ./...\n-race -count=1 (all packages pass, including the new pool-limits\ntests against real testcontainers Postgres), make coverage (99.7%,\ngate 90%), helm lint, helm template smoke render (default/all-enabled/\nmixed).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueY8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbTQQAESPZj9Cyv0dYGvq3O5BbXH/\no1FBZ4NLRipxghL3EyWsykw5c87o+M71ZdvgDN6TIK3hClXPHsnO8g+Fw6MTRhYE\nlanabV6Y8OTf9r/pM10GyvjYCbvo9ZjOiOdhbVqEjvd+mrqe6CnT0iNLgrXRXngB\nQDbuCzYNi18NFgpXP78kVxyQRPvX9UmqFQUNmhh7cWJ6fVKZsXwuULH5O8Cdz1ng\nNtoLXoxJ+5UKrwIz0igBO0lS3+atDfRx2AjjuBwXD3TtH4L8F+TZonc3b/So7qGK\niM7Q7ZqqGFZRdARI90C4UmLSEriolOFCVRAt8b1dXZZM5gvogdA41EFvy6vkV3pr\nK22MY1KzkOsOyszTpHRWQCu+ud9H5P2DyGw2QBhNvaRq6bUWZbamMEDAZxH6EDbU\nnfUZO+kqRTdKXT2X8gexKWBH/DSVxQ1ufEeffii+Hj7kZ1LOQy5zgZgElhquVbKf\nX3Ojgxh4mhJXpZd+crLYFUDW6HFYXR89uUz+8Wfc09tg7tCLFQDEnzC8Vvi+hU+Z\nQcYkWoBNnPqGwovqIUCgs2a6M4xR5zu0S7f/kh3ro+gL2OVNGH2ZW+dVY6y99eK6\n/+nx2d8jZogua/kmmqL2U+uHJ+pwHiqRdJX9qPUeBkLwXp9LstgOzaUfAvkqbAYk\nzX0CPEKpdXbGttN6T/Sb\n=XuN4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:59:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/2d17ff8e594dc831915e37f436100dd993a36ffd","node_id":"C_kwDOUPuTL9oAKDJkMTdmZjhlNTk0ZGM4MzE5MTVlMzdmNDM2MTAwZGQ5OTNhMzZmZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/2474238e7c044ac963c552bf5df241f334e2b588","sha":"2474238e7c044ac963c552bf5df241f334e2b588","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/2474238e7c044ac963c552bf5df241f334e2b588"}],"sha":"2d17ff8e594dc831915e37f436100dd993a36ffd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/2d17ff8e594dc831915e37f436100dd993a36ffd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/2474238e7c044ac963c552bf5df241f334e2b588/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:34:55Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:34:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kafka): switch outbound writers'' Balancer from LeastBytes to Hash (ADR 0013) (#78)\n\ninternal/adapters/outbound/kafka''s Publisher and AnalyticsPublisher have\nalways set kafkago.Message.Key correctly (PathId, or SiteId for\nCPTScheduleChanged) via Encode/AnalyticsEncoder.Encode. That looked\ncorrect by inspection, but both writers were constructed with\nBalancer: &kafkago.LeastBytes{}, which ignores Message.Key entirely when\nrouting to a partition (it balances purely by cumulative byte volume).\nThis was accidentally safe at 1 partition per topic; warehouse-infra\nPR #42 (already merged into develop) took every business topic,\nincluding both of this service''s own topics, from 1 to 8 partitions,\nso the per-PathId (per-SiteId) event ordering this service''s own Encode\ndoc comment promises was never actually being enforced against a real\nbroker.\n\nThis is the same bug found and fixed in order-management (PR #111,\nADR 0027), inventory-storage (PR #102), and workforce-management\n(PR #106) via a fleet-wide audit. This repo''s Key-setting logic was\nalready correct everywhere (confirmed both publish call sites use\nenc.Key, not a freshly-derived key) so only the Balancer needed to\nchange.\n\nChanges:\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher.go: NewPublisher''s writer\n  Balancer -> &kafkago.Hash{}\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/analytics_publisher.go:\n  NewAnalyticsDirectPublisher''s writer Balancer -> &kafkago.Hash{}\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher_balancer_integration_test.go\n  (new, //go:build integration): real-broker Testcontainers test on an\n  8-partition topic proving 3 events for the same PathId land on the\n  same partition while a different PathId''s event is free to land\n  elsewhere. Verified this test fails under the old LeastBytes balancer\n  (1 of 3 same-key messages landed on the majority partition) and\n  passes under Hash — a fake-writer unit test alone could not catch\n  this class of bug since it has no concept of a Balancer.\n- docs/docs/adr/0013-kafka-writer-hash-balancer.md (new): ADR recording\n  the decision, referencing order-management PR #111 and\n  warehouse-infra PR #42.\n- docs/docs/adr/about.md, docs/sidebars.ts: register ADR 0013.\n\nVerified locally: go build/vet, gofmt -l (clean), make check, make\narch-test (including TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers), go\ntest -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1, make coverage (99.7%,\ngate 90%), and docs/ npm run build (Docusaurus, onBrokenLinks: throw).\n\nNo wire-format change; Message.Key is Kafka metadata only.","tree":{"sha":"312922a8be11e7998070ce284ce4187e0df0ff87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/312922a8be11e7998070ce284ce4187e0df0ff87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/2474238e7c044ac963c552bf5df241f334e2b588","verification":{"payload":"tree 312922a8be11e7998070ce284ce4187e0df0ff87\nparent f08f381a397aae1b75600f73f2b9f285deab7104\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790566495 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790566495 -0300\n\nfix(kafka): switch outbound writers'' Balancer from LeastBytes to Hash (ADR 0013) (#78)\n\ninternal/adapters/outbound/kafka''s Publisher and AnalyticsPublisher have\nalways set kafkago.Message.Key correctly (PathId, or SiteId for\nCPTScheduleChanged) via Encode/AnalyticsEncoder.Encode. That looked\ncorrect by inspection, but both writers were constructed with\nBalancer: &kafkago.LeastBytes{}, which ignores Message.Key entirely when\nrouting to a partition (it balances purely by cumulative byte volume).\nThis was accidentally safe at 1 partition per topic; warehouse-infra\nPR #42 (already merged into develop) took every business topic,\nincluding both of this service''s own topics, from 1 to 8 partitions,\nso the per-PathId (per-SiteId) event ordering this service''s own Encode\ndoc comment promises was never actually being enforced against a real\nbroker.\n\nThis is the same bug found and fixed in order-management (PR #111,\nADR 0027), inventory-storage (PR #102), and workforce-management\n(PR #106) via a fleet-wide audit. This repo''s Key-setting logic was\nalready correct everywhere (confirmed both publish call sites use\nenc.Key, not a freshly-derived key) so only the Balancer needed to\nchange.\n\nChanges:\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher.go: NewPublisher''s writer\n  Balancer -> &kafkago.Hash{}\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/analytics_publisher.go:\n  NewAnalyticsDirectPublisher''s writer Balancer -> &kafkago.Hash{}\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher_balancer_integration_test.go\n  (new, //go:build integration): real-broker Testcontainers test on an\n  8-partition topic proving 3 events for the same PathId land on the\n  same partition while a different PathId''s event is free to land\n  elsewhere. Verified this test fails under the old LeastBytes balancer\n  (1 of 3 same-key messages landed on the majority partition) and\n  passes under Hash — a fake-writer unit test alone could not catch\n  this class of bug since it has no concept of a Balancer.\n- docs/docs/adr/0013-kafka-writer-hash-balancer.md (new): ADR recording\n  the decision, referencing order-management PR #111 and\n  warehouse-infra PR #42.\n- docs/docs/adr/about.md, docs/sidebars.ts: register ADR 0013.\n\nVerified locally: go build/vet, gofmt -l (clean), make check, make\narch-test (including TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers), go\ntest -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1, make coverage (99.7%,\ngate 90%), and docs/ npm run build (Docusaurus, onBrokenLinks: throw).\n\nNo wire-format change; Message.Key is Kafka metadata only.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueBfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAilgQAJMHZ5pIayadC8zIylxGIZVL\npg/0P9oXl5rFFwkuWyP7q3xAqFnPxgeqA2HIooJPCFRDv24TF5jv5VbaI6spFSok\n0Kw9cuvkHH+Zem0nvBDHMbI3DHC+CfwhXmgo7GP1mnCacoPxz1OfT1QE4dNv1nyh\ne/TS2qd7jEWgg8/+HuFIr2OtwtfsjdXYaexj7R5l7NbU04adwiSASwgZ10fNihpc\nlmp8yvlVmc9IulpvxNZUxKjS8GbGHqhl46fVquDSguTNPr3g9SGCV1N5Ff8qhF33\n5wdDlHhz2nWrhDD/fgmMY1t7UPGnP01HsxZ2i/h1FNDuRPHtnqt9au6AipaSsX7l\nCzjfSEdDZkcmBrIlTl06pcFWhIJoGfcCBuhMDgnSwghv+ZfkterkaGMwK0kNT3VI\nQNP2VwnlvrjCcaM8hvixTD3khoeU357h/2A7bBYpmJT++KHGYJ6LCBVV8euF72jN\nLnl0Bowz5DT7gy3WNu0Wg6FsKGsE4hjMDlwnPcflzHpS7luCYoqkpEwWIqQbukx1\noMzBga/Np2EDJsj/Uh3VsbX126I6UKbFOhdsBNsBUI4bESvuq8npa1LonaY2Ixhn\n9HoUrzWWx0670fLncDej1O54nJnCxHeOcpyYQlcpluRsSOZMbH9LEKqxyhF093r6\n3EpGllANnVqhGaxcPi9V\n=GidD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:34:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://a