//api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/f08f381a397aae1b75600f73f2b9f285deab7104/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T01:40:27Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T01:40:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(complexity): enforce gocyclo/gocognit/cyclop/funlen/nestif gate, refactor all violations (#77)\n\nEnable the five complexity linters in .golangci.yml (gocyclo 15, gocognit 20,\ncyclop 15 / package-average 10, funlen 80 lines/50 statements, nestif 5;\n_test.go exempt from funlen/gocyclo, web/ exempt from all five) and add a\ndedicated `complexity` CI job (golangci-lint --enable-only + gocyclo report\nin the step summary, gated into docker-publish). Refactor every\npre-existing violation with zero behavior change: table-driven problem\ncatalogs, split wiring/relay/policy functions, named test helpers instead\nof t.Run closures. golangci-lint, go build/vet, go test ./... all green.","tree":{"sha":"e84fdb312e142005077ade950bf30b1c3d6b6b93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/e84fdb312e142005077ade950bf30b1c3d6b6b93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/f08f381a397aae1b75600f73f2b9f285deab7104","verification":{"payload":"tree e84fdb312e142005077ade950bf30b1c3d6b6b93\nparent e3b56708610ed6e96372f192bcdcb7fdf28cef99\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790559627 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790559627 -0300\n\nci(complexity): enforce gocyclo/gocognit/cyclop/funlen/nestif gate, refactor all violations (#77)\n\nEnable the five complexity linters in .golangci.yml (gocyclo 15, gocognit 20,\ncyclop 15 / package-average 10, funlen 80 lines/50 statements, nestif 5;\n_test.go exempt from funlen/gocyclo, web/ exempt from all five) and add a\ndedicated `complexity` CI job (golangci-lint --enable-only + gocyclo report\nin the step summary, gated into docker-publish). Refactor every\npre-existing violation with zero behavior change: table-driven problem\ncatalogs, split wiring/relay/policy functions, named test helpers instead\nof t.Run closures. golangci-lint, go build/vet, go test ./... all green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqucWLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATkAQADz2OVzqnNra9LSamwsd4q0u\ni//saA9ASJuCjJAX2OsOBt3jEqyjZypvw2u1Rxt1FU+/204mRUVyh2uwds6V3Jds\nKlOhEROKCBMAd8FST7viKwteFNKYPIeezgc8uKMXPOjDgMJgeqHKg17r42v2G7eP\nz+X6JXf54Nm2DS7yKeCUkE4F5V3pFa2sWCYf/6HsYYPNC5GIBl387eVKoorMQx9c\n+/RsCLAfnqJVyraCSYe9zsC9V89aS1eEgZHrTw5O/riH/nZ+2gKKorBPQn8knaVs\nsRAg7SnORMQyC+YAzna5SOsvXvD2eXGIKOhaar0+Bw3IL/LwYvat8tHqP6+8/ud0\nUOFAZZpyaqHmphU1licvBlviNA2gGUf0dR6Ccx+hBzUa1velvavJIuJtgakilEiS\nSCba22McL+Ja+U6UNF83qtwSrzKetU2yDLBwtsD0tZEqOg7upNpsGnOvXN6LdwqL\nhwCWbdtCVc49HCHme2dM0tta2uTDMTUssKJCllzYPLV/kIEGk5HGJZAOXQ4xAb2S\n8ABRSKd/PUXh9xprXnRlY1Ik8eX/i3IiBQevJpRtYpP9VgVulhIv/ZOGh2eS/xC2\noSj4+3XRr/i+3s0SElVlVYYsKGon3WbTlBhU9oV7sqs7S/pF1mR/c/F6P2LCTnWh\nf7jbonNL2PDa3hgqHVH5\n=pXt/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T01:40:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/f08f381a397aae1b75600f73f2b9f285deab7104","node_id":"C_kwDOUPuTL9oAKGYwOGYzODFhMzk3YWFlMWI3NTYwMGY3M2YyYjlmMjg1ZGVhYjcxMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/e3b56708610ed6e96372f192bcdcb7fdf28cef99","sha":"e3b56708610ed6e96372f192bcdcb7fdf28cef99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/e3b56708610ed6e96372f192bcdcb7fdf28cef99"}],"sha":"f08f381a397aae1b75600f73f2b9f285deab7104","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/f08f381a397aae1b75600f73f2b9f285deab7104"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/e3b56708610ed6e96372f192bcdcb7fdf28cef99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T22:56:06Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T22:56:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resilience): Kafka DLQ for analytics consumer + graceful shutdown hardening (#76)\n\nPorts order-management''s PR #107 / ADR-0025 DLQ and graceful-shutdown\npatterns into process-path-management (ADR 0012). No circuit breaker\nwork: this service has no sync outbound HTTP calls to any sibling\nbounded context (confirmed by internal/architecture''s\nTestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls fitness test), so there is nothing to\nwrap in a breaker.\n\nKafka consumer DLQ (internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/analytics_consumer.go):\n- cmd/pathmgmt (the OLTP API) has no inbound Kafka consumer at all —\n  documented as a finding in ADR 0012, no DLQ work applies there.\n- The analytics projector''s consumer (cmd/pathmgmt-projector) is the\n  ONLY inbound consumer in this repo. It previously had no dead-letter\n  handling: a permanent failure was logged and silently skipped, with\n  the offset already auto-committed (ReadMessage) by the time the error\n  was even logged.\n- New handleFetchedMessage retries MarkProcessed and the projection\n  apply SEPARATELY (cenkalti/backoff/v4, max 3 attempts each) rather\n  than retrying the whole handler as one unit, because this consumer''s\n  idempotency gate and projection apply are two independent Postgres\n  transactions (unlike order-management''s RepromiseConsumer, where\n  dedupe+mutate is one atomic unit safe to retry wholesale).\n- On exhausting both retry budgets, the raw message plus error-context\n  headers (x-dlq-source-topic/x-dlq-error/x-dlq-failed-at, mirroring\n  RepromiseConsumer''s header shape) is published to <topic>.dlq and the\n  offset is committed anyway, so one poison message never blocks the\n  partition.\n- Switched Run from auto-commit ReadMessage to FetchMessage +\n  explicit CommitMessages, required to control exactly when an offset\n  advances.\n- Proven with a real testcontainers Kafka\n  (analytics_consumer_dlq_integration_test.go): a poison message lands\n  on .dlq after 3 attempts with full context, and a healthy message\n  published right after it is projected without delay.\n\nGraceful shutdown hardening (both composition roots):\n- cmd/pathmgmt: new inboundhttp.Readiness gate backs GET /readyz\n  (distinct from the existing GET /healthz liveness probe). Shutdown\n  order: flip not-ready -> drain HTTP -> stop the outbox relay cleanly\n  -> close the pgx pool LAST.\n- cmd/pathmgmt-projector: new package-private readinessGate backs a new\n  GET /readyz on the admin port. Shutdown order: flip not-ready -> drain\n  the admin server -> cancel the consumer AND WAIT (bounded) for its\n  Run goroutine to actually finish (previously fire-and-forget, racing\n  the goroutine) -> close the Kafka reader/DLQ writer -> close the pgx\n  pool LAST (previously an immediate defer, racing the consumer).\n- Helm chart: readinessProbe on both the OLTP API and the projector\n  deployments now points at /readyz (liveness stays /healthz, since it\n  must never flip during a graceful drain). Added\n  terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30 to both deployments (previously\n  unset). cmd/mcp and cmd/pathmgmt-reports are unchanged — read-only,\n  stateless, nothing to drain.\n\ngo.mod: cenkalti/backoff/v4 (already present transitively, v4.3.0,\nmatching order-management''s version) promoted to a direct dependency\nvia go mod tidy.\n\nVerification:\n- go build/vet, plain and -tags=integration: clean.\n- gofmt: clean.\n- make check (fmt-check, vet, build, lint, test): pass.\n- make arch-test: pass, including TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers\n  and TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls.\n- go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1: pass (real Postgres +\n  real Kafka via testcontainers).\n- make coverage: 99.7% (gate 90%).\n- make bdd: pass.\n- docs build (npm run build): pass.\n\nADR: docs/docs/adr/0012-kafka-dlq-and-graceful-shutdown.md","tree":{"sha":"ca1b2fbf19974a67c57516b35a89f4cc893325fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/ca1b2fbf19974a67c57516b35a89f4cc893325fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/e3b56708610ed6e96372f192bcdcb7fdf28cef99","verification":{"payload":"tree ca1b2fbf19974a67c57516b35a89f4cc893325fe\nparent 603a3e845c251a1124a99898895b41cd56092f7b\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790549766 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790549766 -0300\n\nfeat(resilience): Kafka DLQ for analytics consumer + graceful shutdown hardening (#76)\n\nPorts order-management''s PR #107 / ADR-0025 DLQ and graceful-shutdown\npatterns into process-path-management (ADR 0012). No circuit breaker\nwork: this service has no sync outbound HTTP calls to any sibling\nbounded context (confirmed by internal/architecture''s\nTestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls fitness test), so there is nothing to\nwrap in a breaker.\n\nKafka consumer DLQ (internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/analytics_consumer.go):\n- cmd/pathmgmt (the OLTP API) has no inbound Kafka consumer at all —\n  documented as a finding in ADR 0012, no DLQ work applies there.\n- The analytics projector''s consumer (cmd/pathmgmt-projector) is the\n  ONLY inbound consumer in this repo. It previously had no dead-letter\n  handling: a permanent failure was logged and silently skipped, with\n  the offset already auto-committed (ReadMessage) by the time the error\n  was even logged.\n- New handleFetchedMessage retries MarkProcessed and the projection\n  apply SEPARATELY (cenkalti/backoff/v4, max 3 attempts each) rather\n  than retrying the whole handler as one unit, because this consumer''s\n  idempotency gate and projection apply are two independent Postgres\n  transactions (unlike order-management''s RepromiseConsumer, where\n  dedupe+mutate is one atomic unit safe to retry wholesale).\n- On exhausting both retry budgets, the raw message plus error-context\n  headers (x-dlq-source-topic/x-dlq-error/x-dlq-failed-at, mirroring\n  RepromiseConsumer''s header shape) is published to <topic>.dlq and the\n  offset is committed anyway, so one poison message never blocks the\n  partition.\n- Switched Run from auto-commit ReadMessage to FetchMessage +\n  explicit CommitMessages, required to control exactly when an offset\n  advances.\n- Proven with a real testcontainers Kafka\n  (analytics_consumer_dlq_integration_test.go): a poison message lands\n  on .dlq after 3 attempts with full context, and a healthy message\n  published right after it is projected without delay.\n\nGraceful shutdown hardening (both composition roots):\n- cmd/pathmgmt: new inboundhttp.Readiness gate backs GET /readyz\n  (distinct from the existing GET /healthz liveness probe). Shutdown\n  order: flip not-ready -> drain HTTP -> stop the outbox relay cleanly\n  -> close the pgx pool LAST.\n- cmd/pathmgmt-projector: new package-private readinessGate backs a new\n  GET /readyz on the admin port. Shutdown order: flip not-ready -> drain\n  the admin server -> cancel the consumer AND WAIT (bounded) for its\n  Run goroutine to actually finish (previously fire-and-forget, racing\n  the goroutine) -> close the Kafka reader/DLQ writer -> close the pgx\n  pool LAST (previously an immediate defer, racing the consumer).\n- Helm chart: readinessProbe on both the OLTP API and the projector\n  deployments now points at /readyz (liveness stays /healthz, since it\n  must never flip during a graceful drain). Added\n  terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30 to both deployments (previously\n  unset). cmd/mcp and cmd/pathmgmt-reports are unchanged — read-only,\n  stateless, nothing to drain.\n\ngo.mod: cenkalti/backoff/v4 (already present transitively, v4.3.0,\nmatching order-management''s version) promoted to a direct dependency\nvia go mod tidy.\n\nVerification:\n- go build/vet, plain and -tags=integration: clean.\n- gofmt: clean.\n- make check (fmt-check, vet, build, lint, test): pass.\n- make arch-test: pass, including TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers\n  and TestNoSiblingContextOutboundCalls.\n- go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1: pass (real Postgres +\n  real Kafka via testcontainers).\n- make coverage: 99.7% (gate 90%).\n- make bdd: pass.\n- docs build (npm run build): pass.\n\nADR: docs/docs/adr/0012-kafka-dlq-and-graceful-shutdown.md","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquZ8GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWXEQAAfW4oT/xWlDpzbIGOspAcQ+\njUdH9+pIR3nxb2xaCFor58h2IUZrXtuzDsO0w+7OBKnioBOCAlJ+IM34CD7hPUwc\noq+1T4HNkbEQPgb8vI+xvsn5aBA9dGUyRpQrqNnR2s+yJGyn5exZbi4JcSugu16k\n0Oa/f6VBEwhuUbMobV2MPcyEVuP59nnjU66yxcjY3XQEVkykoZ72MFVz80d5wS9x\nxQjzHkjHpROyWlN6c0BOuw5PVwx5n7v661Hiq9Phco8CVOUBEtxPxoGjH7zsu8NC\nBa+8bxkm9x/8sxxOP1NeKNK/ELkJf+Q7KIn8kcZvc8tm7Tb7nSRST/cEReP7979C\nt9m52OQJ1LYRzXeT7RxYjRYo9McOh37WSEXjusO1bk+oPK/FdSCrs1fQQxC/FyxW\nUx/3hwbLWcMeY1LdVoiwBpMC6Vmz2w/7/IPdbwdkOnm2l1fr8KWcYLitSD+dmafW\n10oDtQSd0BBTMrbEguK+BbnZof1ojj7cVfvs4Gw0yTi3GSVlHPM1pPueGX1yQIOS\nt1JMtuxN5CLX1MWmUMXECRDBWhAqG73epy8UY4BYoRSWrzu3JtjZCJX7u4cyGUQG\nYkmycQTsfHeWLeJuZv1RmA8Puyqi9OUNGfdJP/ptyWXkFpUtNYTU7FaZzB9NbDkm\nMDXdckpxKMag/K3t6arg\n=G1Dx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T22:56:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/e3b56708610ed6e96372f192bcdcb7fdf28cef99","node_id":"C_kwDOUPuTL9oAKGUzYjU2NzA4NjEwZWQ2ZTk2MzcyZjE5MmJjZGNiN2ZkZjI4Y2VmOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/process-path-management/commit/603a3e845c251a1124a99898895b41cd56092f7b","sha":"603a3e845c251a1124a99898895b41cd56092f7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/603a3e845c251a1124a99898895b41cd56092f7b"}],"sha":"e3b56708610ed6e96372f192bcdcb7fdf28cef99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/e3b56708610ed6e96372f192bcdcb7fdf28cef99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/603a3e845c251a1124a99898895b41cd56092f7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:02:31Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:02:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(http): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware for POST /process-paths (#70)\n\nAdds a route-scoped (chi r.With, never r.Use) transactional\nIdempotency-Key middleware protecting the one true resource-creation\nendpoint, DefinePath. This ports order-management''s reference design\n(ADR 0023) to this repo; see ADR 0011 for the full rationale, including\nthe resolved caller-supplied-id question: PathId here is caller-supplied\n(unlike order-management''s server-generated order id), so DefinePath\nalready rejects a duplicate id with a natural-key 409. The middleware is\nstill wired in, because it turns that ambiguous natural-key conflict on\nretry into a clean, response-preserving idempotent replay instead.\n\n- internal/pgtx: new tiny package extracting the transaction-in-context\n  mechanism (WithTx/TxFrom) out of unit_of_work.go''s private\n  withTx/txFrom, so the inbound HTTP middleware and the outbound\n  UnitOfWork can share one transaction without either adapter package\n  importing the other (architecture fitness tests forbid that).\n  unit_of_work.go''s withTx/txFrom now delegate to pgtx unchanged in\n  behavior for every existing caller.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency.go: RequireIdempotencyKey\n  middleware. Missing header -> 400. Begins a pgx transaction, INSERTs\n  the key row (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING) inside it; 1 row -> runs the real\n  handler against a response recorder inside that same tx-bound context,\n  then UPDATEs the row with the outcome and commits before writing to\n  the real ResponseWriter (so a committed row''s status_code is never\n  NULL); 0 rows -> the request already resolved (Postgres'' own\n  unique-index lock guarantees this), so a plain read either replays the\n  cached response verbatim (hash match) or returns 422 (hash mismatch).\n  A panic rolls back and re-panics; its outcome is never cached.\n- cmd/pathmgmt/main.go, server.go: wire IdempotencyPool (the same\n  pgxpool.Pool already opened for persistence) onto POST /process-paths\n  only; skipped entirely when no transactional Postgres backing is\n  configured (in-memory dev/test mode), matching this repo''s existing\n  optional-capability convention.\n- migrations/0006_idempotency_keys: the idempotency_keys table plus a\n  created_at index reserved for a future TTL cleanup job (deferred, not\n  built here).\n- idempotency_integration_test.go: all six required scenarios against a\n  real testcontainers Postgres through the real chi router — fresh key\n  creates the path; replay with the same key+body returns the identical\n  response with exactly one process_paths row; same key + different\n  body -> 422; missing header -> 400; five real concurrent goroutines\n  with the same key -> exactly one path created; a business-validation\n  422 is cached and replayed verbatim on retry.\n- docs/docs/adr/0011, README.md, docs/docs/adr/about.md: ADR and doc\n  updates (endpoint table, curl walkthrough, ADR index).\n\nDefinePath already wrapped Save+Publish in atomically()/UnitOfWork from\nthe transactional-outbox rollout (ADR 0003, PR #7) — no use-case change\nwas needed for the join to work; UnitOfWork.Execute''s existing\n\"already in a transaction? just run fn(ctx)\" branch picks up the\nmiddleware''s pgtx-bound context unmodified.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration) clean, gofmt -l .\nclean, make check and make arch-test green, go test -tags=integration\n./... -race -count=1 green (testcontainers Postgres, no env-var skip,\nno hardcoded localhost), make bdd green, coverage 96.8% -> 99.7%\n(gate: 90%).","tree":{"sha":"1424e43b91100e29fe148ffb93a3013d8118e050","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/1424e43b91100e29fe148ffb93a3013d8118e050"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/603a3e845c251a1124a99898895b41cd56092f7b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1424e43b91100e29fe148ffb93a3013d8118e050\nparent 28f3b655dbc2b4e01892390eb49d49607e48ed10\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790514151 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790514151 -0300\n\nfeat(http): transactional Idempotency-Key middleware for POST /process-paths (#70)\n\nAdds a route-scoped (chi r.With, never r.Use) transactional\nIdempotency-Key middleware protecting the one true resource-creation\nendpoint, DefinePath. This ports order-management''s reference design\n(ADR 0023) to this repo; see ADR 0011 for the full rationale, including\nthe resolved caller-supplied-id question: PathId here is caller-supplied\n(unlike order-management''s server-generated order id), so DefinePath\nalready rejects a duplicate id with a natural-key 409. The middleware is\nstill wired in, because it turns that ambiguous natural-key conflict on\nretry into a clean, response-preserving idempotent replay instead.\n\n- internal/pgtx: new tiny package extracting the transaction-in-context\n  mechanism (WithTx/TxFrom) out of unit_of_work.go''s private\n  withTx/txFrom, so the inbound HTTP middleware and the outbound\n  UnitOfWork can share one transaction without either adapter package\n  importing the other (architecture fitness tests forbid that).\n  unit_of_work.go''s withTx/txFrom now delegate to pgtx unchanged in\n  behavior for every existing caller.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/idempotency.go: RequireIdempotencyKey\n  middleware. Missing header -> 400. Begins a pgx transaction, INSERTs\n  the key row (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING) inside it; 1 row -> runs the real\n  handler against a response recorder inside that same tx-bound context,\n  then UPDATEs the row with the outcome and commits before writing to\n  the real ResponseWriter (so a committed row''s status_code is never\n  NULL); 0 rows -> the request already resolved (Postgres'' own\n  unique-index lock guarantees this), so a plain read either replays the\n  cached response verbatim (hash match) or returns 422 (hash mismatch).\n  A panic rolls back and re-panics; its outcome is never cached.\n- cmd/pathmgmt/main.go, server.go: wire IdempotencyPool (the same\n  pgxpool.Pool already opened for persistence) onto POST /process-paths\n  only; skipped entirely when no transactional Postgres backing is\n  configured (in-memory dev/test mode), matching this repo''s existing\n  optional-capability convention.\n- migrations/0006_idempotency_keys: the idempotency_keys table plus a\n  created_at index reserved for a future TTL cleanup job (deferred, not\n  built here).\n- idempotency_integration_test.go: all six required scenarios against a\n  real testcontainers Postgres through the real chi router — fresh key\n  creates the path; replay with the same key+body returns the identical\n  response with exactly one process_paths row; same key + different\n  body -> 422; missing header -> 400; five real concurrent goroutines\n  with the same key -> exactly one path created; a business-validation\n  422 is cached and replayed verbatim on retry.\n- docs/docs/adr/0011, README.md, docs/docs/adr/about.md: ADR and doc\n  updates (endpoint table, curl walkthrough, ADR index).\n\nDefinePath already wrapped Save+Publish in atomically()/UnitOfWork from\nthe transactional-outbox rollout (ADR 0003, PR #7) — no use-case change\nwas needed for the join to work; UnitOfWork.Execute''s existing\n\"already in a transaction? just run fn(ctx)\" branch picks up the\nmiddleware''s pgtx-bound context unmodified.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration) clean, gofmt -l .\nclean, make check and make arch-test green, go test -tags=integration\n./... -race -count=1 green (testcontainers Postgres, no env-var skip,\nno hardcoded localhost), make bdd green, coverage 96.8% -> 99.7%\n(gate: 90%).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRPnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaOQQAC567XJUmKFl2TtqIQ/qRb8a\npPkgOksh3obmqMuR6/fZ0ThpoAAs4zyAZAHlx/E9ktGJF6pbYLCGz1zQIo7r6RUB\nUPMtCcu5D0kfNbPSOebORThJ7yu8RybPP7Z2LMSPeWwrQfh8ZZDpXeK3OZ9ZRMJq\nciTT96E2IOUiR++ueQ6i7U0VqeNm1xm14cb4WRS9kjTCfUO6YBpPeII0kVx72WOh\neTLdhTU0gZLXF4tQwjVr3D7WOFARKvxFB1htY9Sw9vq6DLSJBd0jTQ5ntzpwgBpB\nmESPkXDLrzq0KJjUapWBCaO3pMFDJneciu7BTx3ZFaUNfCF+GUfv1FdGleoD+M5/\no9LgMCAUj+YTASNAQ82p2zNzhB2ChdrvxV32Ontse0PxeulwZTyNJ9+unMP3HPTy\nEniP41pNWNrr/eRFgITZ7rnB+Z3/PuqWyjeAQM8quFvE08Vuogbs6V4QhOEehwJd\n43CDbTKjLufwBApEV4nFuwstSgo5DZLGM6DAbuhquihw8CM6POnTCOYPi75/u5uz\nYGh7l//1Sj9WyU0nDUO7YOoK81z7okxFJW+D6lcB2zvaqT4e0iUqgRlQk9zTAz7y\nNSdZYnycS5YpKlQ+qbCmqLouhr4Gq3G8s2AaP3XjI7LbeAOQ/TLOjUbOFrT92+0l\nXl/3uN8GCFpvPsBrGPjQ\n=AH7Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T13:02:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subsc