-path-management/commits/98df642557629cf504de9463e539afae3e6e20a0"}],"sha":"5d9485f8b81e86bea78c4e3a5d58f80af2bc5184","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/5d9485f8b81e86bea78c4e3a5d58f80af2bc5184"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/commits/98df642557629cf504de9463e539afae3e6e20a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:24:01Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:24:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(boot): retry Postgres dial at startup with bounded backoff (#65)\n\nAll four process-path-management binaries (pathmgmt, pathmgmt-projector,\npathmgmt-reports, mcp) dial Postgres eagerly at boot (migrations + a\npool.Ping health check). In a fresh cluster rollout, the Postgres\nStatefulSet/pod can still be starting when these binaries start, causing\nan immediate crash instead of a graceful wait — a boot-time crash loop.\n\nAdd internal/adapters/outbound/bootretry: a small bounded-retry helper\n(Do / DoWithDelay) wrapping the dial+ping+migrate sequence with a capped\nbackoff budget of ~31s total, honoring context cancellation. Wire it into\nall four cmd/*/main.go entrypoints around the existing Postgres bootstrap\ncode; no behavioral change once Postgres is reachable.\n\nKafka is intentionally out of scope here: this repo''s kafka-go\nWriter/Reader clients are lazy — they don''t dial until the first\nread/write — and the projector''s Kafka consumer goroutine does not\nos.Exit on failure, so there is no boot-time crash-loop risk from Kafka\nin this service. Only the eager Postgres dial needed the retry wrap.\n\nAdd a startupProbe to the Helm chart (charts/process-path-management) for\nall four deployments (api, mcp, analytics-projector, analytics-reports),\nmirroring network-fulfillment''s chart: httpGet /healthz on the existing\nhealth port, periodSeconds=2, failureThreshold=30 (~60s budget), safely\npast the retry helper''s own ~31s budget. This gives the kubelet a longer\nstartup grace window before liveness/readiness probing (and any\nrestart-on-failure policy) takes over, so pods aren''t killed while still\nwaiting out the bounded Postgres retry.\n\nWired the same way the existing livenessProbe/readinessProbe blocks are\n(`{{- with .Values.startupProbe }}...{{- end }}`) so it''s a no-op unless\nthe value is set (it now always is, by default).\n\nVerified: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./... -race, go build\n-tags=integration ./..., make check, and helm lint / helm template all\npass; `helm template` output confirms all four Deployments render a\nstartupProbe block.","tree":{"sha":"0ebdd66a77f81c92ac2ebca5a17d27f59d246beb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/0ebdd66a77f81c92ac2ebca5a17d27f59d246beb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/98df642557629cf504de9463e539afae3e6e20a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ebdd66a77f81c92ac2ebca5a17d27f59d246beb\nparent 00752a4c14931cf9bc3caf29b37648855c16ba41\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790465041 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790465041 -0300\n\nfix(boot): retry Postgres dial at startup with bounded backoff (#65)\n\nAll four process-path-management binaries (pathmgmt, pathmgmt-projector,\npathmgmt-reports, mcp) dial Postgres eagerly at boot (migrations + a\npool.Ping health check). In a fresh cluster rollout, the Postgres\nStatefulSet/pod can still be starting when these binaries start, causing\nan immediate crash instead of a graceful wait — a boot-time crash loop.\n\nAdd internal/adapters/outbound/bootretry: a small bounded-retry helper\n(Do / DoWithDelay) wrapping the dial+ping+migrate sequence with a capped\nbackoff budget of ~31s total, honoring context cancellation. Wire it into\nall four cmd/*/main.go entrypoints around the existing Postgres bootstrap\ncode; no behavioral change once Postgres is reachable.\n\nKafka is intentionally out of scope here: this repo''s kafka-go\nWriter/Reader clients are lazy — they don''t dial until the first\nread/write — and the projector''s Kafka consumer goroutine does not\nos.Exit on failure, so there is no boot-time crash-loop risk from Kafka\nin this service. Only the eager Postgres dial needed the retry wrap.\n\nAdd a startupProbe to the Helm chart (charts/process-path-management) for\nall four deployments (api, mcp, analytics-projector, analytics-reports),\nmirroring network-fulfillment''s chart: httpGet /healthz on the existing\nhealth port, periodSeconds=2, failureThreshold=30 (~60s budget), safely\npast the retry helper''s own ~31s budget. This gives the kubelet a longer\nstartup grace window before liveness/readiness probing (and any\nrestart-on-failure policy) takes over, so pods aren''t killed while still\nwaiting out the bounded Postgres retry.\n\nWired the same way the existing livenessProbe/readinessProbe blocks are\n(`{{- with .Values.startupProbe }}...{{- end }}`) so it''s a no-op unless\nthe value is set (it now always is, by default).\n\nVerified: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./... -race, go build\n-tags=integration ./..., make check, and helm lint / helm template all\npass; `helm template` output confirms all four Deployments render a\nstartupProbe block.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquFQRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfB4QALFWzJOqjvfEii+swfCmR7Xk\neUd2M9tKIc90XfkjjvJXXXnhKeO3KdLGWmZ3qcnOwgwFiMqMiIDfCovvtdHPZxCy\nRlOWfXKMC7K4Uugj8l6iw0MLeeqeRAJkPpN0y4Y1bxhTYboQ9ihpG05SlXblf70S\nKkJEtlAArm8QPT7H3DRROA5d22PouHPD3OG+AfZFA7YL612K/fufOMp5VCmNxeQK\nHo144QpGRT+OghwqG/R+zL0TgIdwQVNHmICd+t9Ps7OlIiJg6vKg1drX3MS90vf/\ntQcZgJP4CQlZdGVvP3GcsGRlNaG2MfwwYG4G8n1FuwsTMPOM3QELE7kpwugnevkc\nXi1QnhR4Jc3+GOMs/WLtE0xHi8ZsXrF3aqJzevngSVevUkpK9PlnFBuolIQlqgT3\n7rsDrWqggTXSSAsKAjArVqDsF0I2CTqTfK518MPPLv1mbG6ZuRk5JzB7Ag3MMJIR\n0kg29UQd86Do3mQGouiUnTPii4Ee4CEH144kl8pVwA35N8sMsLj2A3On0cvm1HAA\n1TnRKsQ6K+Q5lAYTuhdugF7whUPYXyQcdTFs3LmQk5XLFcvAjheBg/42S4JHSdG0\nKHL/fpAqxX4GEg2FMwMwJ7KybHVwR/yqwAMdFMSRagKJgexWkT4qC0ayPYl2x6V/\nmZvlYueuQph0HK/IGl/v\n=mM0r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T23:24:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://ap