ease notes) with\n  `ghcr.io/`.\n- Update the couple of docs/README lines that named Docker Hub as the\n  registry.\n\nSame trigger, same versioning scheme (SHORT_SHA + :latest on main,\nsemver tag on release) -- registry only.","tree":{"sha":"79f923229aa4e23724c82d872d42d0ec70382efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/trees/79f923229aa4e23724c82d872d42d0ec70382efe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/process-path-management/git/commits/a1ffbf594f617bee412a991eac6788d4c152632d","verification":{"payload":"tree 79f923229aa4e23724c82d872d42d0ec70382efe\nparent b09781fb3e5cbd058ef8e3fb9174ddd6b9dbca85\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790429351 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790429351 -0300\n\nci(docker-publish): publish images to GHCR instead of Docker Hub (#60)\n\nSwitch docker-publish and release jobs from Docker Hub to GHCR:\n- Replace the Docker Hub login step (DOCKERHUB_USERNAME/DOCKERHUB_TOKEN)\n  with a GHCR login using the built-in GITHUB_TOKEN (no new secret needed).\n- Add `packages: write` to docker-publish''s job permissions (required to\n  push to GHCR).\n- Prefix every image reference (build tags, cosign sign/attest, SBOM\n  attestation, imagetools re-tag on release, release notes) with\n  `ghcr.io/`.\n- Update the couple of docs/README lines that named Docker Hub as the\n  registry.\n\nSame trigger, same versioning scheme (SHORT_SHA + :latest on main,\nsemver tag on release) -- registry only.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt8inCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYhYQAHL0eUmYmRkDMz/30jtMeAZe\nEdq9ynBRK4IyQwuLHHR5FXUx8DrmI8VHRUqDhg7aqq/k6/Bhg4TxXzh+OMmDw46F\nPlBqK8ngwp6goghafnX3OmQ0t2i8xLs6vM+ZDb2kLNl2dG5mtNT1xF+f3ZQxGeBd\nFR5r9Z/sS15BCg2WAwtYUmeNcjZ4Ay0i5ypZ0r+KpZb95etFRAsm9hsGuBUMMsAB\n6gyglN8PH1rLipXCYPMRv+rfUhVx2Rgd5UETO+jFO33QchenKPEGWwqfx2ptdHfQ\ncijPbFlQAgNNHG6unCBAzMyc6X2D0rH2774mgMv091E92VMTkvwAXjsgsR8Xplta\nGjvuVwix1Eek7xLyqtOqqt5