criptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/websterwh/breaker-box/commit/1ef242c29a89296f4869d250d45b16777ea84d7d","node_id":"C_kwDOUP27ENoAKDFlZjI0MmMyOWE4OTI5NmY0ODY5ZDI1MGQ0NWIxNjc3N2VhODRkN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/websterwh/breaker-box/commit/438986372c7448e3d2ab43b821f0c01d8a433ea5","sha":"438986372c7448e3d2ab43b821f0c01d8a433ea5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/websterwh/breaker-box/commits/438986372c7448e3d2ab43b821f0c01d8a433ea5"}],"sha":"1ef242c29a89296f4869d250d45b16777ea84d7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/websterwh/breaker-box/commits/1ef242c29a89296f4869d250d45b16777ea84d7d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81191122?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/websterwh","id":81191122,"login":"websterwh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTkxMTIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/websterwh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/websterwh/breaker-box/commits/438986372c7448e3d2ab43b821f0c01d8a433ea5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:31:42Z","email":"websterwh16@gmail.com","name":"William"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:31:42Z","email":"websterwh16@gmail.com","name":"William"},"message":"Expand global toggle to also cover the Worker''s own auto-detect, restyle as a switch\n\nClarified: \"global toggle\" meant covering ALL automatic behavior, not\njust the container watcher and auto-push - including the Worker''s own\nbuilt-in auto-detect fallback (showing Restarting/Offline pages when\nMODE isn''t manually set and the origin looks unreachable).\n\n- worker/src/index.js: new optional AUTO_FEATURES_ENABLED secret - \"0\"\n  skips autoDetect() entirely and passes the request straight through\n  with no interception, as if this Worker weren''t there. Only affects\n  the no-MODE-set path; manual MODE=M/MODE=R are never touched by this.\n- Plugin: applyAutoFeaturesToggle() pushes/clears that secret whenever\n  the switch changes, alongside the existing settings.json field the\n  watcher already reads directly.\n- Replaced the plain checkbox with an actual switch control (track +\n  thumb, native checkbox underneath for keyboard/screen-reader support)\n  per request - verified all four track/thumb/background colour pairs\n  clear the 3:1 non-text contrast threshold.\n\nLocal wrangler dev can''t exercise the new branch meaningfully (self-\nfetch recursion with no bound real origin, the same known limitation\nfrom earlier in this session) - verified by code review instead: a\none-line early return ahead of the existing autoDetect() call, and the\nenv-var-reading mechanism itself was already proven repeatedly via the\nCONTAINER_WATCH_AT tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HfaStgU9JpiYKj3KKfC1u9","tree":{"sha":"ace4f379544f67866bc611cfee4395f7b3bc0b46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/websterwh/breaker-box/git/trees/ace4f379544f67866bc611cfee4395f7b3bc0b46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/websterwh/breaker-box/git/commits/438986372c7448e3d2ab43b821f0c01d8a433ea5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified