.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/commits/50a0f2195fcd304cbcfb253c1cb615f86af77485/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:53:21Z","email":"tonmoy.ashik@gmail.com","name":"ashikMostofaTonmoy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:53:21Z","email":"tonmoy.ashik@gmail.com","name":"ashikMostofaTonmoy"},"message":"Part 5+6: real VPC networking, public/private subnets, NAT, RDS, ALB\n\n- infra/40-vpc.sh: custom VPC (10.0.0.0/16), 6 subnets across 2 AZs\n  (public x2, private-app x2, private-db x2), IGW, public route table.\n- infra/41-nat-gateway.sh: NAT Gateway + EIP + private route table, so\n  private subnets get outbound-only internet access.\n- infra/42-security-groups.sh: one SG per tier (alb/frontend/backend/db),\n  chained so each only accepts the hop before it -- no SSH rule anywhere,\n  SSM needs no inbound port at all.\n- infra/43-rds.sh: managed PostgreSQL via RDS, private, not publicly\n  accessible, in a DB subnet group spanning both AZs.\n- infra/44-ec2-instances.sh: frontend (public in Class 5, private in\n  Class 6 via --frontend-subnet) + backend (always private) EC2, plus a\n  small S3 bucket both read via SSM for all deploys -- no SSH/scp anywhere\n  in this module, even where SSH would technically reach the frontend.\n- infra/45-alb.sh: Application Load Balancer + target group (health check\n  /healthz) -- the only public entry point once the frontend goes private.\n- scripts/deploy-{db,backend,frontend}-vpc.sh: same app as Parts 1-2,\n  shipped entirely over SSM send-command.\n- scripts/deploy-monitoring-vpc.sh: Part 3/4''s stack relocated -- exporters\n  on the frontend (scraped over its private IP, not localhost), everything\n  else on the backend, postgres_exporter pointed at the RDS endpoint.\n- backend/src/db.js: RDS requires SSL by default; node-postgres doesn''t\n  turn it on from DATABASE_URL alone -- added a PGSSL env flag (Part 2''s\n  local Postgres is unaffected).\n- infra/teardown-vpc.sh: reverses everything; found live that the four\n  security groups reference each other (a real cycle) and naive one-by-one\n  deletion deadlocks -- revokes every rule on all four first, then deletes.\n- README: sections 39-58, two more classes'' worth of material -- VPC/subnet\n  theory, NAT, security-group chaining (with a live stateful-connections\n  gotcha proven by a negative test), RDS, cross-instance monitoring, ALB/\n  target groups, and full end-to-end verification through the ALB with the\n  alert-fire demo replayed on the new topology.\n\nVerified live end-to-end against profile ostad: both classes'' full request\npaths proven (browser -> Nginx -> Node -> RDS, across 3 separate hosts),\nall 7 monitoring targets UP including 2 cross-instance ones, a security-group\nnegative test (revoke then force-reconnect then restore), and the\nBackendDown alert firing/resolving on this topology. Everything torn down\nand re-verified empty after.","tree":{"sha":"b1f830e3d4f48b3f899c1174897f009589b0005d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/git/trees/b1f830e3d4f48b3f899c1174897f009589b0005d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/git/commits/50a0f2195fcd304cbcfb253c1cb615f86af77485","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43008495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashikMostofaTonmoy","id":43008495,"login":"ashikMostofaTonmoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMDA4NDk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/commit/50a0f2195fcd304cbcfb253c1cb615f86af77485","node_id":"C_kwDOUQShfNoAKDUwYTBmMjE5NWZjZDMwNGNiY2ZiMjUzYzFjYjYxNWY4NmFmNzc0ODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/commit/3e9d119c9a619155dd6cec34ff1aaab38d8a4a25","sha":"3e9d119c9a619155dd6cec34ff1aaab38d8a4a25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/commits/3e9d119c9a619155dd6cec34ff1aaab38d8a4a25"}],"sha":"50a0f2195fcd304cbcfb253c1cb615f86af77485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/commits/50a0f2195fcd304cbcfb253c1cb615f86af77485"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43008495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashikMostofaTonmoy","id":43008495,"login":"ashikMostofaTonmoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMDA4NDk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/commits/3e9d119c9a619155dd6cec34ff1aaab38d8a4a25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:24:53Z","email":"tonmoy.ashik@gmail.com","name":"ashikMostofaTonmoy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:24:53Z","email":"tonmoy.ashik@gmail.com","name":"ashikMostofaTonmoy"},"message":"Part 3+4: monitoring, visualization, and alerting (Prometheus, Grafana, Loki)\n\n- backend/src/metrics.js: prom-client HTTP + business metrics\n  (weather_search_requests_total, weather_current_temperature_celsius).\n  Each PM2 cluster worker exposes its own /metrics on 9200+NODE_APP_INSTANCE\n  -- found live that scraping the shared app port would silently see only\n  whichever worker answered a given connection, since each worker has its\n  own in-process registry.\n- backend/src/logger.js: structured JSON logs via pino (was console.log).\n- monitoring/: prometheus.yml, alert-rules.yml (InstanceDown, BackendDown,\n  PostgresDown, HighCPULoad, HighMemoryUsage, DiskSpaceLow), Alertmanager\n  config (Slack receiver), Loki + Promtail configs, Grafana datasource\n  provisioning files, and a custom three-tier-app-dashboard.json split into\n  Server vs Application rows.\n- scripts/deploy-monitoring.sh: installs node_exporter, nginx-exporter,\n  postgres_exporter, Prometheus, Alertmanager, Loki, Promtail, and Grafana\n  as systemd services, idempotently. Grafana moved to port 3001 (3000\n  collides with the backend). Promtail pinned to v3.5.0 -- Loki dropped it\n  from releases after that (Grafana is steering users to Alloy instead).\n- infra/30-monitoring-sg.sh: opens 9090/9093 (caller''s IP only -- no auth on\n  those UIs) and 3001 (public -- Grafana has a login) on the existing SG.\n- README: sections 22-38, two new classes'' worth of material -- monitoring\n  fundamentals, PromQL, Grafana, custom dashboards, server vs application\n  metrics, logs as a third pillar, and a live alert-fire-and-resolve demo\n  with real Prometheus/Alertmanager/Loki output.\n\nVerified live end-to-end against profile ostad: all 8 services active, all\n6 Prometheus targets UP, dashboards rendering real data, BackendDown alert\nobserved Pending -> Firing -> resolved in both Prometheus and Alertmanager,\ncorrelated against real Loki log lines for the same window.","tree":{"sha":"ccf73fa15218be2fc248382b0e1c9377a1e5e368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/git/trees/ccf73fa15218be2fc248382b0e1c9377a1e5e368"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ashikMostofaTonmoy/three-tier-deployment/git/commits/3e9d119c9a619155dd6cec34ff1aaab38d8a4a25","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43008495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashikMostofaTonmoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashikMostofaTonmoy","id":43008495,"login":"ashikMo