https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/b66ff8955c2c288a59f4d13b6d8537b82026da9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:05:37Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:05:37Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Add Granola integration — import meeting notes into an event''s Learnings\n\nChecked Granola''s real docs before building anything (same discipline as\nthe LinkedIn integration): a personal API key (Settings -> Connectors ->\nAPI keys in the Granola app), no OAuth needed — a plain bearer token,\nsame simple pattern already used for the Luma iCal URL.\n\n- 0005_granola.sql: user_settings.granola_api_key, plus a\n  granola_note_imports tracking table (not a single column on events) —\n  by design, one event can have several associated Granola notes over\n  time (e.g. a pre-call and the event itself), so this is a proper\n  many-to-one, not a single latest-import slot\n- granola-search-notes: finds candidate notes in a +/-3 day window around\n  an event''s start time (a pre-call or follow-up is still worth\n  surfacing, not just an exact-day match), sorted by proximity, flagging\n  ones already imported for this event\n- granola-import-note: fetches one note''s AI summary and appends it to\n  the event''s Learnings (never replaces, per the multi-note design),\n  recording the import so it won''t show as importable again\n- Settings: a Granola card (paste API key, masked like a real secret)\n- Event detail: a \"Find Granola notes\" button opens a modal (same\n  conditionally-mounted pattern as the LinkedIn share dialog) listing\n  candidates with per-row Import buttons\n\nOne honest caveat, called out in code comments: Granola''s docs describe\nthe note-summary field only as \"an AI-generated overview,\" without\nquoting the literal JSON key, and no live API key was available to\nverify a real response while building this. granola-import-note checks\na few plausible field names and returns a clear, explicit error if none\nmatch, rather than silently importing nothing — first real test will\nconfirm whether that guess needs adjusting.","tree":{"sha":"d6311639af93094412bede877c04daf59b2e5bdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/d6311639af93094412bede877c04daf59b2e5bdb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/b66ff8955c2c288a59f4d13b6d8537b82026da9d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/b66ff8955c2c288a59f4d13b6d8537b82026da9d","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKGI2NmZmODk1NWMyYzI4OGE1OWY0ZDEzYjZkODUzN2I4MjAyNmRhOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/11d39a62a0746f4a20e2ca0058afea6d03bb091f","sha":"11d39a62a0746f4a20e2ca0058afea6d03bb091f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/11d39a62a0746f4a20e2ca0058afea6d03bb091f"}],"sha":"b66ff8955c2c288a59f4d13b6d8537b82026da9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/b66ff8955c2c288a59f4d13b6d8537b82026da9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/11d39a62a0746f4a20e2ca0058afea6d03bb091f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:52:28Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:52:28Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Actually fix the truncation: escape LinkedIn''s reserved rich-text characters\n\nRoot cause, finally confirmed with an exact before/after comparison from\na real post: the draft in the edit box was complete, but what published\ncut off at precisely the first \"(\" — a plain parenthetical remark, not a\nlength or generation issue at all. The previous two fixes (removing then\nexplicitly disabling thinking/effort) were solving the wrong problem;\nthis was never about token budgets.\n\nLinkedIn''s Posts API \"commentary\" field isn''t plain text — it''s their own\n\"little\" rich-text format (mentions, hashtags, bold/italic), documented\nto reserve \\ | { } @ [ ] ( ) < > * _ ~. Per LinkedIn''s own docs: \"All\nreserved characters need to be escaped with a backslash, even if those\ncharacters are not used in one of the supported elements or templates.\"\nAn unescaped \"(\" in ordinary prose has no valid parse as a mention or\nanything else, and the parser silently drops everything after it rather\nthan erroring — which is exactly the silent, no-error truncation\nreported.\n\nAdded escapeLittleText(), applied to commentary right before the Posts\nAPI call. # is deliberately left unescaped, since a bare #word is\ngenuinely how LinkedIn renders a real clickable hashtag, and this app''s\nown drafts always end with a few — escaping it would turn every\nintentional hashtag into inert text. Verified against the exact real\ndraft text that triggered this bug: parentheses now escape correctly,\nhashtags at the end stay live.","tree":{"sha":"7366ea47fc3f18bb0ebee6bb573490feca3d6fe0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/7366ea47fc3f18bb0ebee6bb573490feca3d6fe0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/11d39a62a0746f4a20e2ca0058afea6d03bb091f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/11d39a62a0746f4a20e2ca0058afea6d03bb091f","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDExZDM5YTYyYTA3NDZmNGEyMGUyY2EwMDU4YWZlYTZkMDNiYjA5MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/1ebfe4dcdd01aa67e09e4a5cd7bdcc733eb9bbab","sha":"1ebfe4dcdd01aa67e09e4a5cd7bdcc733eb9bbab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/1ebfe4dcdd01aa67e09e4a5cd7bdcc733eb9bbab"}],"sha":"11d39a62a0746f4a20e2ca0058afea6d03bb091f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/11d39a62a0746f4a20e2ca0058afea6d03bb091f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/1ebfe4dcdd01aa67e09e4a5cd7bdcc733eb9bbab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:38:57Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:38:57Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Actually fix the truncation bug: explicitly disable thinking, don''t just omit effort\n\nPrevious fix (removing output_config.effort entirely) didn''t work because\nClaude Sonnet 5 defaults to \"high\" effort on the API when output_config\nis omitted (confirmed in Anthropic''s docs) — silently reverting to a\n*higher* default than the \"medium\" it replaced, not disabling anything.\nHigh effort still thinks on anything the model judges non-trivial (e.g.\na multi-speaker panel with several discussion threads to synthesize),\nand thinking tokens share the same max_tokens budget as the visible\nresponse — so the real LinkedIn post that got cut off after \"removing\"\neffort was actually thinking *more*, not less.\n\nFixed properly this time: thinking: {type: ''disabled''} (confirmed valid\nsyntax in Anthropic''s docs) deterministically guarantees zero reasoning-\ntoken overhead, rather than relying on a lower effort level \"usually\"\nskipping thinking for simple problems. Paired with effort: ''low'' for\nconciseness on top. Both draft-linkedin-post and summarize-learnings\nredeployed.","tree":{"sha":"a227be76bd46137bb9c6c949a53d2efc26f6bd77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/a227be76bd46137bb9c6c949a53d2efc26f6bd77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/1ebfe4dcdd01aa67e09e4a5cd7bdcc733eb9bbab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/1ebfe4dcdd01aa67e09e4a5cd7bdcc733eb9bbab","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDFlYmZlNGRjZGQwMWFhNjdlMDllNGE1Y2Q3YmRjYzczM2ViOWJiYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/a4c3402a2dea4464ea0f48017c235059bc1d3255","sha":"a4c3402a2dea4464ea0f48017c235059bc1d3255","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/a4c3402a2dea4464ea0f48017c235059bc1d3255"}],"sha":"1ebfe4dcdd01aa67e09e4a5cd7bdcc733eb9bbab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/1ebfe4dcdd01aa67e09e4a5cd7bdcc733eb9bbab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/a4c3402a2dea4464ea0f48017c235059bc1d3255/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:29:37Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:29:37Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Fix LinkedIn drafts (and monthly summaries) getting truncated mid-response\n\nRoot cause, confirmed against a real published-then-cut-off LinkedIn post\nand Anthropic''s own docs: output_config.effort only does anything when\npaired with thinking: {type: \"adaptive\"}, and thinking tokens count\nagainst the same max_tokens budget as the visible response. Both\ndraft-linkedin-post and summarize-learnings set effort: ''medium'' alone\n(no thinking config) with max_tokens: 1024 — for a model where that\nimplicitly engages some adaptive thinking, this silently ate into the\nbudget meant for the actual output, cutting the LinkedIn draft off\nmid-sentence. Neither task needs any reasoning depth in the first place\n(short, straightforward text generation), so the fix drops effort\nentirely rather than tuning it, plus a higher max_tokens (1536) as\nheadroom.\n\nAlso added \"Post again\" next to \"View on LinkedIn\" once an event has\nalready been posted — for when the original post gets deleted on\nLinkedIn itself and there''s currently no way back into the share flow.\nDrafts and posts fresh, overwriting the stored post urn/timestamp with\nthe new one.","tree":{"sha":"06ec96ec95490a6c1ac115e215eba61d3e12c179","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/06ec96ec95490a6c1ac115e215eba61d3e12c179"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/a4c3402a2dea4464ea0f48017c235059bc1d3255","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/a4c3402a2dea4464ea0f48017c235059bc1d3255","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKGE0YzM0MDJhMmRlYTQ0NjRlYTBmNDgwMTdjMjM1MDU5YmMxZDMyNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/895515d44b0cdff69c4fbf890b697264815da3df","sha":"895515d44b0cdff69c4fbf890b697264815da3df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/895515d44b0cdff69c4fbf890b697264815da3df"}],"sha":"a4c3402a2dea4464ea0f48017c235059bc1d3255","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/a4c3402a2dea4464ea0f48017c235059bc1d3255"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/895515d44b0cdff69c4fbf890b697264815da3df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:19:47Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:19:47Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"LinkedIn draft flow as a modal, custom draft instructions, and two swipe-deck fixes\n\nLinkedIn:\n- \"Share on LinkedIn\" now opens a centered modal (dimmed backdrop, same\n  conditionally-mounted pattern as calendar-view.tsx''s day picker) that\n  drives the whole draft -> edit -> regenerate -> post flow, instead of an\n  inline expanding section on the page\n- 0004_linkedin_post_instructions.sql: user_settings.linkedin_post_instructions\n  (free text) — Settings'' LinkedIn card now has a \"Post writing\n  instructions\" textarea (tone, intro requirements, anything standing);\n  draft-linkedin-post fetches it and folds it into the system prompt,\n  explicitly told to override the generic guidance where they conflict\n\nSwipe deck (Dashboard):\n- Cards are now centered and width-capped (420px) on wide screens instead\n  of stretching full desktop width above the still-blurred calendar;\n  narrow stays full-bleed since there''s no spare width to center within\n- Fixed the WENT/DID NOT GO badge visually covering the corner X/check\n  buttons — both occupied the same top-corner region (badge top:20 vs.\n  button top:12), and the badge''s own rotation pushed its bounding box out\n  even further into the button zone. Badges now sit below the buttons\n  entirely (top:68) instead of nearly on top of them.","tree":{"sha":"e09361d3aff5c7ee8315811e0dc7a3ad016b3464","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/e09361d3aff5c7ee8315811e0dc7a3ad016b3464"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/895515d44b0cdff69c4fbf890b697264815da3df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/895515d44b0cdff69c4fbf890b697264815da3df","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDg5NTUxNWQ0NGIwY2RmZjY5YzRmYmY4OTBiNjk3MjY0ODE1ZGEzZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/81dbed52c8032bfa2c32e8afe892b6527beb3a2d","sha":"81dbed52c8032bfa2c32e8afe892b6527beb3a2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/81dbed52c8032bfa2c32e8afe892b6527beb3a2d"}],"sha":"895515d44b0cdff69c4fbf890b697264815da3df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/895515d44b0cdff69c4fbf890b697264815da3df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/81dbed52c8032bfa2c32e8afe892b6527beb3a2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:06:49Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:06:49Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Fix LinkedIn OAuth popup never closing on web\n\nRoot cause, confirmed against a real failed connection attempt (popup\nnever closed; manually closing it reported \"cancelled\") and against\nexpo-web-browser''s actual web implementation (node_modules, not just its\ndocs): on web, openAuthSessionAsync does NOT poll the popup''s URL from\nthe opener — that''s blocked cross-origin regardless. It waits for the\nredirect page itself to call WebBrowser.maybeCompleteAuthSession(), which\nreads the pending redirect out of localStorage and postMessages it back\nto window.opener. linkedin-callback.tsx never called this, so there was\nno code path that could ever complete the connection automatically — not\na timing issue, nothing was going to finish it regardless of how long the\npopup sat open.\n\nThis still requires testing from the exact origin registered as the\nOAuth redirect URI (https://luma-brief.vercel.app) rather than\nlocalhost — the postMessage handshake needs the popup and opener to\nshare localStorage, which only happens same-origin.","tree":{"sha":"4673506665c814f13a6bfb817f921f66d7762f05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/4673506665c814f13a6bfb817f921f66d7762f05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/81dbed52c8032bfa2c32e8afe892b6527beb3a2d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/81dbed52c8032bfa2c32e8afe892b6527beb3a2d","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDgxZGJlZDUyYzgwMzJiZmEyYzMyZThhZmU4OTJiNjUyN2JlYjNhMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/9a971db2016db578d69ceacb7636ec74dc71c9e7","sha":"9a971db2016db578d69ceacb7636ec74dc71c9e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/9a971db2016db578d69ceacb7636ec74dc71c9e7"}],"sha":"81dbed52c8032bfa2c32e8afe892b6527beb3a2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/81dbed52c8032bfa2c32e8afe892b6527beb3a2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/9a971db2016db578d69ceacb7636ec74dc71c9e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:21:09Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:21:09Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Add \"Share on LinkedIn\" — draft from Learnings, edit, post\n\nVerified the actual current LinkedIn API shape before writing any code\n(OAuth 2.0 + OpenID Connect endpoints, and the Posts API which replaced\nthe deprecated ugcPosts API) rather than relying on possibly-stale\nknowledge, since this touches a real external service.\n\n- 0003_linkedin.sql: linkedin_connections table (one OAuth access token\n  per user, ~60-day lifetime — LinkedIn''s self-serve tier has no refresh\n  token, so periodic reconnecting is expected) + linkedin_post_urn/\n  linkedin_posted_at on events, so a shared post can be shown/reopened\n  instead of re-offering Share indefinitely\n- linkedin-connect: exchanges the OAuth code for an access token and\n  resolves the member''s own profile URN (via /v2/userinfo''s `sub` claim)\n  — the only place LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET is ever used\n- draft-linkedin-post: Claude drafts a short, first-person, blog-style\n  post from one event''s real details + its Learnings notes — same\n  architecture as summarize-learnings, reflective tone instead of bullets\n- post-to-linkedin: publishes the (possibly user-edited) final text via\n  LinkedIn''s real Posts API (POST /rest/posts, author = the member''s own\n  URN — never an organization), then records the post URN/timestamp\n- use-linkedin.ts: client hooks, including the OAuth flow via\n  expo-web-browser''s openAuthSessionAsync against a fixed production\n  redirect URL (LinkedIn requires a real https URL, not a custom scheme —\n  same reason Expo Go''s dynamic exp:// couldn''t work for Supabase''s magic\n  link) — works the same way from web or native\n- Settings: Connect/Reconnect LinkedIn card\n- Event detail: \"Share on LinkedIn\" section (only shown once Learnings\n  notes exist) — Draft, edit inline, Regenerate, Post to LinkedIn; shows\n  \"Posted\" + a link to the real post afterward\n\nExternal setup still needed before this can work end-to-end (can''t be\ndone from here — needs the user''s own LinkedIn account): create a\nLinkedIn Company Page + Developer App, request the \"Sign In with\nLinkedIn using OpenID Connect\" and \"Share on LinkedIn\" products, register\nhttps://luma-brief.vercel.app/linkedin-callback as an authorized redirect\nURL, then set EXPO_PUBLIC_LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID (app env + Vercel) and\nLINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID/LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET (supabase secrets set).","tree":{"sha":"76e0d16afdf5bf01cc7daaab3711fe310d4e74f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/76e0d16afdf5bf01cc7daaab3711fe310d4e74f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/9a971db2016db578d69ceacb7636ec74dc71c9e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/9a971db2016db578d69ceacb7636ec74dc71c9e7","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDlhOTcxZGIyMDE2ZGI1NzhkNjljZWFjYjc2MzZlYzc0ZGM3MWM5ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/444ea1f778849488cba632a8fc4b0daea352651c","sha":"444ea1f778849488cba632a8fc4b0daea352651c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/444ea1f778849488cba632a8fc4b0daea352651c"}],"sha":"9a971db2016db578d69ceacb7636ec74dc71c9e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/9a971db2016db578d69ceacb7636ec74dc71c9e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/444ea1f778849488cba632a8fc4b0daea352651c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:44:18Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:44:18Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Add an ambient gradient background to Landing + Sign-in, plus a real footer\n\nScoped to just these two entry pages (per discussion) rather than the\nwhole app — Calendar/Network/Settings rely on clean white backgrounds for\ndata readability, and a colorful ambient gradient behind those risks\nhurting legibility.\n\nNew apps/app/src/components/gradient-background.tsx: fakes the look of\nthe reference \".gradient-bg\" CSS (a blurred, fixed, cover-sized image)\nwithout an actual blur filter or radial-gradient primitive — neither\nexists in React Native. Instead: a few oversized circles, each filled\nwith a linear gradient fading from a brand color to fully transparent,\nwhich reads as a soft glow with no hard edge. Rendered as a sibling\n*before* each screen''s ScrollView (not inside it) so it stays fixed\nbehind scrolling content, the RN equivalent of `position: fixed`.\n\n- index.tsx (Landing): removed the old flat hero-only gradient in favor\n  of this ambient one covering the whole page; step/example cards got\n  explicit opaque backgrounds so they stay legible over it; replaced the\n  one-line footer with a real one (brand, tagline, copyright — no\n  fabricated links to pages that don''t exist)\n- sign-in.tsx: added the same gradient, a header with a \"back to\n  LumaBrief\" link (so users aren''t stranded on this screen), and turned\n  the sign-in card into an actual floating card (opaque surface, border,\n  shadow) instead of bare text sitting directly on the page\n\nVerified in the browser at 1280x900 — zero console errors on both pages.","tree":{"sha":"b3b4fd1ca4dc03a0e99c3fec20dd3837c01cdd3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/b3b4fd1ca4dc03a0e99c3fec20dd3837c01cdd3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/444ea1f778849488cba632a8fc4b0daea352651c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/444ea1f778849488cba632a8fc4b0daea352651c","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDQ0NGVhMWY3Nzg4NDk0ODhjYmE2MzJhOGZjNGIwZGFlYTM1MjY1MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/1c008729710b1773600b2f794c2bf88db54e80f5","sha":"1c008729710b1773600b2f794c2bf88db54e80f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/1c008729710b1773600b2f794c2bf88db54e80f5"}],"sha":"444ea1f778849488cba632a8fc4b0daea352651c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/444ea1f778849488cba632a8fc4b0daea352651c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/1c008729710b1773600b2f794c2bf88db54e80f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:28:48Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:28:48Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Rebuild the landing page as a real product page, not just a hero\n\nModeled structurally on newhereclub.vercel.app (hero -> how-it-works ->\nconcrete example -> final CTA -> footer), adapted to LumaBrief''s own\ncontent and design tokens rather than copying its copy or imagery (none\nof which exist here — this leans on icons, color, and a gradient hero\ninstead of photography):\n\n- Hero: gradient background (reusing the nav bar''s own wash), bigger\n  headline/subhead, pill-shaped CTA with an arrow icon\n- How it works: 3 real, live pillars only (Luma sync, swipe tracking, AI\n  takeaways) — deliberately leaves out Network/LinkedIn since that''s\n  still a parked placeholder, not something to promise on the landing page\n- A concrete before/after example (scattered notes -> AI takeaway) using\n  Fonts.mono for the \"before\" side — the one differentiated thing this\n  app actually does that''s worth showing rather than just describing\n- Repeated final CTA + a minimal footer (no fabricated links to pages\n  that don''t exist, e.g. Terms/Privacy)\n- Responsive via the existing useBreakpoint() hook: steps and the\n  before/after cards stack on narrow, sit in a row on wide\n\nVerified in the browser at 1280x900 and 390x844 — zero console errors at\neither width.","tree":{"sha":"5d54978b995c8051140ae382d9e3cf1d8d406cc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/5d54978b995c8051140ae382d9e3cf1d8d406cc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/1c008729710b1773600b2f794c2bf88db54e80f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/1c008729710b1773600b2f794c2bf88db54e80f5","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDFjMDA4NzI5NzEwYjE3NzM2MDBiMmY3OTRjMmJmODhkYjU0ZTgwZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/03191ac2ba23fdde35c6229ccb14ab627535a599","sha":"03191ac2ba23fdde35c6229ccb14ab627535a599","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/03191ac2ba23fdde35c6229ccb14ab627535a599"}],"sha":"1c008729710b1773600b2f794c2bf88db54e80f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/1c008729710b1773600b2f794c2bf88db54e80f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/03191ac2ba23fdde35c6229ccb14ab627535a599/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:41:46Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:41:46Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Auto-scroll Learnings textarea as it grows from typing alone\n\nautomaticallyAdjustKeyboardInsets only reacts to the keyboard''s own size\nchanging (focus, keyboard show/hide) — confirmed on a real device it does\nNOT re-trigger when the textarea grows a new line while the keyboard\nstays the same size (e.g. repeatedly pressing Enter), leaving new lines\nhidden behind the keyboard with no automatic way to see them.\n\nAdded a ScrollView ref + the TextInput''s onContentSizeChange, scrolling\nto the end of the page whenever the box''s content size changes. Learnings\nis the last section on the page, so \"scroll to the end of the page\" and\n\"scroll to the bottom of this box\" are the same thing — which is also\nexactly where the cursor sits while actively typing.","tree":{"sha":"930ce1512f06d4b234f335db70d693b94f48d0c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/930ce1512f06d4b234f335db70d693b94f48d0c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/03191ac2ba23fdde35c6229ccb14ab627535a599","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/03191ac2ba23fdde35c6229ccb14ab627535a599","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDAzMTkxYWMyYmEyM2ZkZGUzNWM2MjI5Y2NiMTRhYjYyNzUzNWE1OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/572614977793689e91c40d8818c9864a33dde6c3","sha":"572614977793689e91c40d8818c9864a33dde6c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/572614977793689e91c40d8818c9864a33dde6c3"}],"sha":"03191ac2ba23fdde35c6229ccb14ab627535a599","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/03191ac2ba23fdde35c6229ccb14ab627535a599"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/572614977793689e91c40d8818c9864a33dde6c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:26:26Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:26:26Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Fix Learnings textarea still getting cut off by the keyboard\n\nKeyboardAvoidingView only padded the whole screen up once, uniformly —\nconfirmed on a real iPhone it still left the bottom of the growing\nLearnings textarea below the fold with no automatic way to scroll the\nrest of the way into view. Swapped to ScrollView''s\nautomaticallyAdjustKeyboardInsets instead (the officially recommended\napproach over KeyboardAvoidingView for this exact case): it scrolls the\nfocused input into view on focus and keeps following the cursor as the\ntext grows. iOS-only, so added android.softwareKeyboardLayoutMode:\n\"resize\" to app.json as Android''s equivalent (untested — no Android\ndevice in hand yet).","tree":{"sha":"dc27dbf31aa32f498f7dd425fde396c631fb03ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/dc27dbf31aa32f498f7dd425fde396c631fb03ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/572614977793689e91c40d8818c9864a33dde6c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/572614977793689e91c40d8818c9864a33dde6c3","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDU3MjYxNDk3Nzc5MzY4OWU5MWM0MGQ4ODE4Yzk4NjRhMzNkZGU2YzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/dd39845eb87a4b29f6278acb74ef5c9c7880db2a","sha":"dd39845eb87a4b29f6278acb74ef5c9c7880db2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/dd39845eb87a4b29f6278acb74ef5c9c7880db2a"}],"sha":"572614977793689e91c40d8818c9864a33dde6c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/572614977793689e91c40d8818c9864a33dde6c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/dd39845eb87a4b29f6278acb74ef5c9c7880db2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:19:58Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:19:58Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Fix keyboard covering the Learnings textarea on iOS\n\nA plain ScrollView doesn''t push its content above the keyboard on its\nown — the Learnings textarea (the tallest input on the page, and near the\nbottom) ended up hidden behind the keyboard as soon as it was focused.\nWrapped in KeyboardAvoidingView (iOS only; Android already resizes the\nview via windowSoftInputMode) and added keyboardShouldPersistTaps\nso tapping elsewhere on the page doesn''t need an extra tap to dismiss\nthe keyboard first.","tree":{"sha":"4a6b16241de6bfd4bb82dd68182d4bab6a49be3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/4a6b16241de6bfd4bb82dd68182d4bab6a49be3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/dd39845eb87a4b29f6278acb74ef5c9c7880db2a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/dd39845eb87a4b29f6278acb74ef5c9c7880db2a","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKGRkMzk4NDVlYjg3YTRiMjlmNjI3OGFjYjc0ZWY1YzljNzg4MGRiMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/73faa336e278025b0d303dc12cd91c75516d8e71","sha":"73faa336e278025b0d303dc12cd91c75516d8e71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/73faa336e278025b0d303dc12cd91c75516d8e71"}],"sha":"dd39845eb87a4b29f6278acb74ef5c9c7880db2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/dd39845eb87a4b29f6278acb74ef5c9c7880db2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/73faa336e278025b0d303dc12cd91c75516d8e71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:15:41Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:15:41Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Give narrow calendar cells real height instead of aspect-ratio squares\n\ncellNarrow was aspectRatio: 1, sizing each cell''s height off a ~55-60pt-\nwide 1/7-of-screen column — on a real phone that left the whole grid (and\nthe Calendar section as a whole) far shorter than the screen, with a\nlarge dead white gap below the legend. Switched to a fixed minHeight\n(independent of width) and bumped dot size/spacing to match the taller\ncells.","tree":{"sha":"99d74e95223cd195a3a1fb7e7a0f654000eb2109","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/99d74e95223cd195a3a1fb7e7a0f654000eb2109"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/73faa336e278025b0d303dc12cd91c75516d8e71","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/73faa336e278025b0d303dc12cd91c75516d8e71","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDczZmFhMzM2ZTI3ODAyNWIwZDMwM2RjMTJjZDkxYzc1NTE2ZDhlNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/b9eaf342c97236bd3bc46627c64fcdecdf39d6aa","sha":"b9eaf342c97236bd3bc46627c64fcdecdf39d6aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/b9eaf342c97236bd3bc46627c64fcdecdf39d6aa"}],"sha":"73faa336e278025b0d303dc12cd91c75516d8e71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/73faa336e278025b0d303dc12cd91c75516d8e71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/b9eaf342c97236bd3bc46627c64fcdecdf39d6aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T18:16:59Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T18:16:59Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Fix missing safe-area handling on native (header under notch, tabs cut off)\n\nreact-native-safe-area-context was already a transitive dependency but\nnever actually wired up — every screen''s content rendered flush against\nthe physical screen edges. Confirmed on a real iPhone screenshot: the\nDashboard''s \"Calendar\" title rendered underneath the status bar/Dynamic\nIsland, and the bottom tab bar sat flush against the home-indicator area.\n\n- _layout.tsx: wrap the app in SafeAreaProvider so useSafeAreaInsets()\n  resolves real values anywhere below it\n- adaptive-shell.tsx: apply insets.top to the narrow-layout content\n  wrapper (no TopBar there to already clear the notch) and to TopBar''s own\n  padding on wide layouts; apply insets.bottom to BottomTabs so it clears\n  the home-indicator area, with the original 8px kept as a floor on\n  devices with no inset (Android gesture-nav off, older iPhones)\n\nNo change on web (insets resolve to 0 there) — verified narrow-width web\nstill renders with no console errors.","tree":{"sha":"81fec7e73b3358536c94d6eb2432a351e5703082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/81fec7e73b3358536c94d6eb2432a351e5703082"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/b9eaf342c97236bd3bc46627c64fcdecdf39d6aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/b9eaf342c97236bd3bc46627c64fcdecdf39d6aa","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKGI5ZWFmMzQyYzk3MjM2YmQzYmM0NjYyN2M2NGZjZGVjZGYzOWQ2YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/167a2ce8cfc7ba63367bc0a5ad84393079244cb5","sha":"167a2ce8cfc7ba63367bc0a5ad84393079244cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/167a2ce8cfc7ba63367bc0a5ad84393079244cb5"}],"sha":"b9eaf342c97236bd3bc46627c64fcdecdf39d6aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/b9eaf342c97236bd3bc46627c64fcdecdf39d6aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/167a2ce8cfc7ba63367bc0a5ad84393079244cb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:59:35Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:59:35Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Stop hardcoding a 6-digit OTP length\n\nConfirmed against a real received email that this project''s actual email\nOTP length is 8, not 6 — the hardcoded maxLength={6} was silently\ntruncating input, making the code field impossible to submit correctly.\nCopy generalized to \"code\" instead of \"6-digit code\", input cap raised to\na generous 12 (not a real limit, just a guard against pasting garbage),\nand the submit-enable threshold loosened from exactly 6 to >= 4 chars.","tree":{"sha":"8bec4ca1991a26dd6e1681f1af017659cda731ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/8bec4ca1991a26dd6e1681f1af017659cda731ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/167a2ce8cfc7ba63367bc0a5ad84393079244cb5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/167a2ce8cfc7ba63367bc0a5ad84393079244cb5","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDE2N2EyY2U4Y2ZjN2JhNjMzNjdiYzBhNWFkODQzOTMwNzkyNDRjYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/630860fd76e6fdb5368aa8e34478f849ff237e0a","sha":"630860fd76e6fdb5368aa8e34478f849ff237e0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/630860fd76e6fdb5368aa8e34478f849ff237e0a"}],"sha":"167a2ce8cfc7ba63367bc0a5ad84393079244cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/167a2ce8cfc7ba63367bc0a5ad84393079244cb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/630860fd76e6fdb5368aa8e34478f849ff237e0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:55:13Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:55:13Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Add a Remove button to correct a mis-swiped event\n\nShows next to the status pill on the event detail page whenever an\nevent''s status is one that actually appears on the calendar (went/going/\npending). Sets status to did_not_go — the same status that already makes\nan event disappear from both the calendar and the swipe deck — and\nnavigates back once it succeeds so the removal is visible immediately.","tree":{"sha":"aaf00e6d233c2b4428111d321488e53b737f1225","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/aaf00e6d233c2b4428111d321488e53b737f1225"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/630860fd76e6fdb5368aa8e34478f849ff237e0a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/630860fd76e6fdb5368aa8e34478f849ff237e0a","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDYzMDg2MGZkNzZlNmZkYjUzNjhhYThlMzQ0NzhmODQ5ZmYyMzdlMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/87dbe3d86de8b471f603a2e339e5f38a600af560","sha":"87dbe3d86de8b471f603a2e339e5f38a600af560","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/87dbe3d86de8b471f603a2e339e5f38a600af560"}],"sha":"630860fd76e6fdb5368aa8e34478f849ff237e0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/630860fd76e6fdb5368aa8e34478f849ff237e0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/87dbe3d86de8b471f603a2e339e5f38a600af560/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:53:32Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:53:32Z","email":"isabelbolger@hotmail.com","name":"Isabel Bolger"},"message":"Make the 6-digit code the primary sign-in path, not the magic link\n\nRoot cause of \"Token has expired or is invalid\" appearing within a\nminute of the email arriving: the code and the link share one underlying\none-time token, and Outlook/Hotmail''s \"Safe Links\" scanner auto-visits\nevery link in incoming mail to check it for phishing — silently consuming\nthe token before the user ever opens the email. A longer expiry window\nwouldn''t fix this; removing the auto-visitable link does. Copy updated to\nmatch a Magic Link email template with no ConfirmationURL link, code-only\n(see chat for the template HTML) — the deep-link/detectSessionInUrl\nplumbing in auth-context.tsx is left in place but now dormant unless a\nlink gets added back to the template later.","tree":{"sha":"760b27168d4bc1885def44c70afac0126d395e7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/trees/760b27168d4bc1885def44c70afac0126d395e7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/git/commits/87dbe3d86de8b471f603a2e339e5f38a600af560","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18249360?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel","id":18249360,"login":"isa3bel","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjQ5MzYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isa3bel","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/87dbe3d86de8b471f603a2e339e5f38a600af560","node_id":"C_kwDOUQiEZNoAKDg3ZGJlM2Q4NmRlOGI0NzFmNjAzYTJlMzM5ZTVmMzhhNjAwYWY1NjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commit/ab067d265b29ae0b3950ac1d5d80021e60400326","sha":"ab067d265b29ae0b3950ac1d5d80021e60400326","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Luma-Brief/commits/ab067d265b29ae0b3950ac1d5d80021e60400326"}],"sha":"87dbe3d86de8b471f603a2e339e5f38a600af560","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isa3bel/Lu