ancogarayokk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francogarayokk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francogarayokk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francogarayokk/FE_case_study_innoscripta/commits/d0368faa4f965a5dce024655012c0c4fdea58269/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:17:48Z","email":"francogaray94128@gmail.com","name":"francogarayokk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T08:17:48Z","email":"francogaray94128@gmail.com","name":"francogarayokk"},"message":"feat(delivery): price a month from effective-dated rates\n\nImplement the pricing core. rateInForce picks the record that applies\non a given day, monthPricing splits a month into slices at every rate\nchange (the validFrom day itself is priced at the new rate) and\npersonMonth prices an allocation spread evenly over the month''s working\ndays. A month before the employee''s first rate record is reported as\nunpriced rather than silently priced at zero.\n\nSlices are built by walking working days, so a validFrom that falls on\na Saturday starts its slice on the Monday. The blended hourly rate\naverages over all working days with unpriced days weighing zero, which\nkeeps cost and hours exact inverses of each other.\n\nThe tests pin the reference calculation from the brief: emp-001 at\n0.50 person-months in March 2026, 8 days at 80.00 and 14 at 95.00,\ngiving 7,880.00 and a blended rate of 89.5455.","tree":{"sha":"7cce3ddfb83ccf9a163d8673e65ee5e4b0e1b821","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francogarayokk/FE_case_study_innoscripta/git/trees/7cce3ddfb83ccf9a163d8673e65ee5e4b0e1b821"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/francogarayokk/FE_case_study_innoscripta/git/commits/d0368faa4f965a5dce024655012c0c4fdea58269","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com